/* Lecture 1 video lecture data: chapters, slide start times, timed bilingual transcript (generated). */
window.LEC = {"num":1,"videoBase":"https://wabyking.github.io/nlp2026-videos-1/lecture01/","parts":[{"n":1,"title":"Welcome: Your Instructor and the Research Team","blurb":"Who is teaching this course: Benyou Wang's path between academia and industry, the group's open-source work at FreedomIntelligence, and an invitation to join as a research assistant.","file":"lecture01_part1.mp4","poster":"lecture01_part1.jpg","duration":541.6,"first":1,"last":10,"slides":[{"n":1,"title":"Title: Lecture 1","t":0.8},{"n":2,"title":"Contents","t":63.92},{"n":3,"title":"About me – 王本友 Benyou Wang.","t":107.08},{"n":4,"title":"About me 王本友 Benyou Wang.","t":173.22},{"n":5,"title":"Academia or industrial career","t":239.29},{"n":6,"title":"Awards and honour","t":293.51},{"n":7,"title":"We rank 14th in Greater China","t":355.33},{"n":8,"title":"Be Open for AI","t":402.6},{"n":9,"title":"https://github.com/orgs/FreedomIntelligence","t":444.47},{"n":10,"title":"Our team - Join us as a Research Assistant!","t":486.92}],"sents":[[0.8,6.49,1,"Hello everyone, and welcome to Natural Language Processing, Fall two thousand twenty-six.","大家好，欢迎来到自然语言处理课程，2026 年秋季学期。"],[6.84,17.2,1,"Whether you're here as CSC fifty fifty-one, MDS fifty-one ten or CSC sixty fifty-two, you're in the right place, and I'm really glad to see you.","无论你选的是 CSC5051、MDS5110 还是 CSC6052，你都来对地方了，很高兴见到大家。"],[17.55,24.21,1,"Since this is our very first meeting, there's nothing to recap yet, so today is about setting the stage.","这是我们的第一次见面，还没有什么需要回顾的，所以今天主要是搭好舞台。"],[24.56,29.99,1,"I'll tell you a bit about who I am, how this course works, and what I expect from you.","我会先介绍一下我自己、这门课怎么运作，以及我对大家的期望。"],[30.34,34.98,1,"Then we'll get into the real question: what is NLP?","然后我们进入真正的问题：什么是 NLP？"],[35.33,42.67,1,"And how did we get from old-school text processing to the large language models and agents you're already using every day?","我们又是如何从老式的文本处理，一路走到大家每天都在用的大语言模型和智能体的？"],[43.02,48.88,1,"Why does this matter? Language is how humans store and share almost all of our knowledge.","这为什么重要？因为人类几乎所有的知识，都是靠语言来储存和分享的。"],[49.23,56.58,1,"A machine that can really work with language can read, write, reason and act in the world for us.","一台真正能处理语言的机器，就能替我们阅读、写作、推理，并在现实世界中行动。"],[56.93,62.52,1,"That's exactly what's happening right now, and this course is about understanding it from the inside.","这正是此刻正在发生的事情，而这门课就是要带大家从内部理解它。"],[63.77,66.49,2,"Here's the roadmap for today, in four parts.","这是今天的路线图，一共四个部分。"],[66.84,73.05,2,"First, a few minutes about me, so you know who's teaching you and what my group works on.","第一，花几分钟介绍我自己，让大家知道是谁在给你们上课、我的课题组在做什么。"],[73.4,82.57,2,"Second, the philosophy of this course: logistics, grading, assignments, and especially the final project, which is the heart of this class.","第二，这门课的理念：课程安排、评分、作业，尤其是期末项目，它是这门课的核心。"],[82.92,90.87,2,"Third, the actual content: what NLP is, how the field evolved, and how we arrived at large language models and agents.","第三，真正的内容：什么是 NLP，这个领域如何演进，以及我们是怎样走到大语言模型和智能体的。"],[91.22,98.46,2,"And finally, a short tour of some research from our group, to show you what people can actually build with these tools.","最后，简单介绍一下我们组的一些研究，让大家看看用这些工具实际能做出什么。"],[98.81,103.59,2,"The logic is simple: who, how, what, and then what's possible.","逻辑很简单：谁来教、怎么学、学什么，以及能做成什么。"],[103.94,105.68,2,"Let's start with the who.","我们先从“谁”开始。"],[106.93,111.16,3,"A quick introduction. I'm Benyou Wang, or Wang Benyou in Chinese.","简单介绍一下，我是王本友。"],[111.51,119.02,3,"I've been at CUHK-Shenzhen since two thousand twenty-two, as an assistant professor in the School of Data Science.","我从 2022 年起在香港中文大学（深圳）工作，是数据科学学院的助理教授。"],[119.37,124.85,3,"I'm also affiliated with the School of Medicine and the Shenzhen Loop Area Institute.","同时我也在医学院和深圳河套学院任职。"],[125.2,134.42,3,"My research today is basically about agents built on large language models, and you can read this list as the parts of an agent.","我现在的研究基本上围绕基于大语言模型的智能体，这个列表可以看成智能体的各个组成部分。"],[134.77,141.79,3,"Planning is the brain: complex reasoning, math modeling, tool calling, even automatic theorem proving.","规划是大脑：复杂推理、数学建模、工具调用，甚至自动定理证明。"],[142.14,150.47,3,"Perception is the senses: audio, vision and time series, which is where multimodal LLMs come in.","感知是感官：音频、视觉和时间序列，这就是多模态大模型发挥作用的地方。"],[150.82,158.33,3,"Then there's how agents interact with humans, from HCI to agent simulation to brain-computer interfaces.","然后是智能体如何与人交互，从人机交互、智能体仿真到脑机接口。"],[158.68,165.7,3,"And finally applications, especially medicine, but also finance, law and education.","最后是应用，尤其是医疗，也包括金融、法律和教育。"],[166.05,171.82,3,"You'll see many of these themes come back later in the course, so this list is also a small preview.","这些主题很多会在后面的课程里再次出现，所以这个列表也算是一个小小的预告。"],[173.07,178.23,4,"A little more on my path, because it may help some of you think about your own.","再多讲一点我的经历，也许能帮助大家思考自己的道路。"],[178.58,181.38,4,"The timeline runs from left to right.","这条时间线从左往右。"],[181.73,189.97,4,"I started with a master's at Tianjin University, and visited the Institute of Linguistics at the Chinese Academy of Social Sciences.","我在天津大学读硕士，期间访问了中国社会科学院语言研究所。"],[190.32,195.15,4,"Then I worked full-time as a researcher at Tencent.","之后我在腾讯做全职研究员。"],[195.5,203.25,4,"After that I went to Europe as a Marie Curie researcher, and did my PhD at the University of Padua in Italy.","再之后我以玛丽·居里研究员的身份去了欧洲，在意大利帕多瓦大学读博士。"],[203.6,214.48,4,"Along the way there were visits to Copenhagen, Amsterdam and Montreal, an internship at Huawei Noah's Ark Lab, and a visit to the Institute of Theoretical Physics at CAS.","期间我访问过哥本哈根、阿姆斯特丹和蒙特利尔，在华为诺亚方舟实验室实习，还访问过中科院理论物理研究所。"],[214.83,219.14,4,"Why is Galileo on the slide? Because he taught at Padua.","为什么幻灯片上有伽利略？因为他曾在帕多瓦大学任教。"],[219.49,224.64,4,"I like to remind myself that the father of modern science walked the same corridors.","我喜欢提醒自己：“现代科学之父”曾走过同样的走廊。"],[224.99,229.63,4,"The real message: a research career is rarely a straight line.","真正想说的是：科研生涯很少是一条直线。"],[229.98,237.89,4,"Industry, academia, linguistics, physics, all of it ended up feeding into how I think about NLP.","工业界、学术界、语言学、物理学，这些最后都融入了我对 NLP 的思考。"],[239.14,244.83,5,"Since I've been on both sides, people often ask me: should I go to academia or industry?","因为两边我都待过，常有人问我：该去学术界还是工业界？"],[245.18,248.52,5,"Let me share some honest thoughts, not a recommendation.","我分享一些真实的想法，而不是给建议。"],[248.87,255.29,5,"In academia you usually earn less, but you work for yourself, and you're free to pick your topics.","在学术界，收入通常更少，但你是为自己工作，可以自由选择研究方向。"],[255.64,262.78,5,"Your work can benefit society more broadly, rather than one employer, and you also meet very diverse people.","你的工作能更广泛地造福社会，而不只是某一个雇主，你也会认识非常多元的人。"],[263.13,267.76,5,"Long vacations are possible, though in practice you may never take them.","长假是可能的，不过实际上你可能永远不会去休。"],[268.11,272.17,5,"In industry, weekends are usually real weekends.","在工业界，周末通常就是真正的周末。"],[272.52,278.37,5,"And there's less pressure to keep finding funding and keep your research line alive on your own.","而且不用独自承受不断找经费、维持研究方向的压力。"],[278.72,280.91,5,"Neither is better in general.","总体来说，没有哪一个更好。"],[281.26,286.28,5,"The line at the bottom is the one to remember: the best choice is the one that fits you.","要记住的是最下面那句话：最适合你的，才是最好的。"],[286.63,292.11,5,"Think about what motivates you, and use projects like the ones in this course to find out.","想想什么真正驱动你，并用这门课里这样的项目去找到答案。"],[293.36,299.98,6,"Here are a few recognitions our work has received over the years, just so you know the kind of research we do.","这是我们的工作这些年获得的一些认可，让大家了解我们做的是什么样的研究。"],[300.33,310.49,6,"On the NLP and IR side, there's a best paper at NLPCC twenty twenty-two, and an honourable mention for best paper at SIGIR twenty seventeen.","在 NLP 和信息检索方面，有 NLPCC 2022 最佳论文，以及 SIGIR 2017 最佳论文荣誉提名。"],[310.84,316.69,6,"There's also the best explainable NLP paper at NAACL twenty nineteen.","还有 NAACL 2019 最佳可解释 NLP 论文。"],[317.04,324.63,6,"More recently, our TwinMarket work won the best paper at the ICLR twenty twenty-five Financial AI workshop.","最近，我们的 TwinMarket 工作获得了 ICLR 2025 金融 AI 研讨会最佳论文。"],[324.98,333.15,6,"And we had an outstanding paper at a NeurIPS twenty twenty-five workshop on responsible foundation models.","我们还在 NeurIPS 2025 负责任基础模型研讨会上获得了杰出论文。"],[333.5,343.93,6,"I was also supported by an EU Marie Curie fellowship, and we've had support from industry programs at Huawei, Tencent and Didi.","我还获得过欧盟玛丽·居里学者资助，我们也得到过华为、腾讯和滴滴等企业项目的支持。"],[344.28,346.23,6,"I'm not showing this to brag.","我展示这些不是为了炫耀。"],[346.58,353.93,6,"The point is that good work from a small group, including students like you, can get noticed internationally.","重点是：一个小团队、包括像你们这样的学生做出的好工作，也能获得国际认可。"],[355.18,357.25,7,"Here's something I'm quite proud of.","这是一件我很自豪的事。"],[357.6,366.21,7,"This is a snapshot of universities and research groups on Hugging Face, ranked by total likes, taken in November twenty twenty-three.","这是 Hugging Face 上各大学和研究组按总点赞数的排名截图，时间是 2023 年 11 月。"],[366.56,372.45,7,"Look at the highlighted row: FreedomIntelligence, which is our group's organization.","看高亮的这一行：FreedomIntelligence，就是我们课题组的组织。"],[372.8,379.66,7,"At that time we ranked fourteenth on this list, next to groups from much bigger and older institutions.","当时我们在这个榜单上排第十四，旁边都是来自规模更大、历史更久的机构的团队。"],[380.01,385.33,7,"Also notice the datasets column: we release a lot of datasets, not just models.","也请注意数据集这一列：我们发布了很多数据集，而不只是模型。"],[385.68,387.91,7,"The lesson is about openness.","这里的启示是开放。"],[388.26,396.83,7,"A lot of the impact in modern NLP comes from releasing things that other people can actually use: models, data and code.","现代 NLP 的很多影响力，来自发布别人真正能用的东西：模型、数据和代码。"],[397.18,401.2,7,"That's a philosophy I'd like you to take into your own projects too.","我希望大家也把这种理念带到自己的项目里。"],[402.45,406.33,8,"This is exactly that philosophy: be open for AI.","这正是那个理念：为 AI 保持开放。"],[406.68,409.83,8,"There are two websites you'll use constantly in this course.","这门课里有两个网站你会经常用到。"],[410.18,415.2,8,"Hugging Face is where you find datasets, pretrained models and trending papers.","Hugging Face 是你找数据集、预训练模型和热门论文的地方。"],[415.55,417.3,8,"GitHub is where you find code.","GitHub 是你找代码的地方。"],[417.65,420.7,8,"Our group's pages on both are listed at the bottom.","我们组在这两个平台上的主页列在最下面。"],[421.05,427.6,8,"We have over a million model downloads on Hugging Face, and over ten thousand stars on GitHub across our projects.","我们在 Hugging Face 上的模型下载量超过一百万，在 GitHub 上各项目合计超过一万颗星。"],[427.95,433.66,8,"If you're not yet comfortable with these two platforms, please fix that in the first couple of weeks.","如果你还不熟悉这两个平台，请在开学头两周内补上。"],[434.01,443.07,8,"Almost every assignment and final project will start like this: find a model on Hugging Face, find some code on GitHub, and build on top of it.","几乎每个作业和期末项目都会这样开始：在 Hugging Face 上找模型，在 GitHub 上找代码，然后在此基础上搭建。"],[444.32,448.99,9,"This is a glimpse of our GitHub organization, sorted roughly by stars.","这是我们 GitHub 组织的一个缩影，大致按星数排序。"],[449.34,453.4,9,"You don't need to read every line, but notice the range.","不需要逐行看，但请注意它的覆盖面。"],[453.75,460.25,9,"There are medical models like the HuatuoGPT family, and a large open medical skills library.","有像 HuatuoGPT 系列这样的医疗模型，还有一个大型开源医疗技能库。"],[460.6,469.66,9,"There's multimodal work like ALLaVA and LongLLaVA, plus benchmarks, datasets, game and agent projects, and curated paper lists.","有 ALLaVA、LongLLaVA 这样的多模态工作，还有评测基准、数据集、游戏和智能体项目，以及整理好的论文列表。"],[470.01,474.79,9,"Many of these started as student projects, some even as course projects.","其中很多最初是学生项目，有些甚至就是课程项目。"],[475.14,479.48,9,"If any of these interests you, they're good starting points.","如果你对其中哪个感兴趣，它们都是很好的起点。"],[479.83,485.52,9,"You can read the code, reproduce a result, or extend one of them for your final project.","你可以读代码、复现结果，或者把其中一个扩展成你的期末项目。"],[486.77,492.34,10,"And if you want to go deeper than the course, our team is recruiting research assistants.","如果你想比课程走得更深，我们团队正在招研究助理。"],[492.69,500.81,10,"What you get: GPU resources and access to plenty of LLM APIs, and close interaction with the research team.","你能得到：GPU 计算资源和充足的大模型 API，以及与研究团队的密切交流。"],[501.16,508.02,10,"There's a real chance at co-authoring papers, and possibly a paid part-time contract with office space.","有真实的机会合作发表论文，还可能获得带薪的兼职合同和办公位。"],[508.37,516.99,10,"We also give internship recommendations to places like Microsoft, Qwen, the big Chinese tech companies, Huawei and ByteDance.","我们还会推荐实习，比如微软、Qwen、国内互联网大厂、华为和字节跳动。"],[517.34,524.25,10,"What we expect is serious commitment: at least thirty hours a week, and solid programming skills.","我们期望的是认真投入：每周至少三十小时，以及扎实的编程能力。"],[524.6,527.68,10,"To be honest, it also comes with more pressure.","说实话，压力也会更大。"],[528.03,532.95,10,"If you're interested, email me or my colleague at the addresses on the slide.","如果感兴趣，请按幻灯片上的邮箱联系我或我的同事。"],[533.3,539.72,10,"Finishing a strong final project in this course is also a very good way to show us what you can do.","在这门课里完成一个出色的期末项目，也是向我们展示你能力的好方式。"]]},{"n":2,"title":"How the Course Works: Logistics, Structure and Grading","blurb":"The practical side of the course: staff, schedule, what an advanced graduate deep dive means, the week-by-week structure and how the components of your grade fit together.","file":"lecture01_part2.mp4","poster":"lecture01_part2.jpg","duration":485.6,"first":11,"last":21,"slides":[{"n":11,"title":"Contents","t":0.8},{"n":12,"title":"Logistics","t":24.55},{"n":13,"title":"Previous TA：考虑做RSI方向的创业 Recursive Self-improvement","t":75.92},{"n":14,"title":"Logistics","t":112.78},{"n":15,"title":"This is an advanced graduate course and we will be offering a deep dive into the field and equip students with the compr","t":157.24},{"n":16,"title":"Course Structure (tentative)","t":208.64},{"n":17,"title":"Course Structure (tentative)","t":265.42},{"n":18,"title":"Course Structure (tentative)","t":306.97},{"n":19,"title":"Course Structure (tentative)","t":344.81},{"n":20,"title":"Course Structure (tentative)","t":382.78},{"n":21,"title":"Components and Grading (Post-Graduate)","t":421.5}],"sents":[[0.8,5.39,11,"Enough about me. Let's move to the second part: the philosophy of this course.","关于我就说到这里。我们进入第二部分：这门课的理念。"],[5.74,8.09,11,"This part answers practical questions.","这一部分回答一些实际问题。"],[8.44,13.63,11,"How is the course organized? How will you be graded? What do the assignments look like?","课程是怎么组织的？怎么评分？作业是什么样的？"],[13.98,23.15,11,"And most importantly, how should you approach the final project, which is where most of your learning, and most of your grade, will come from?","最重要的是，该如何对待期末项目？你大部分的收获和大部分的成绩都来自它。"],[24.4,26.15,12,"First, the basics.","先说基本信息。"],[26.5,33.6,12,"I'm the instructor, and we have a strong team of teaching assistants, with Shunian Chen as the leading TA.","我是主讲老师，我们有一支很强的助教团队，陈舒年是首席助教。"],[33.95,38.18,12,"Their photos are here so you can recognize them around campus.","这里放了他们的照片，方便大家在校园里认出他们。"],[38.53,43.24,12,"Please do talk to them; they've all been through this kind of research themselves.","请多和他们交流，他们自己都做过这类研究。"],[43.59,51.31,12,"We meet on Fridays from one thirty to four twenty in the afternoon, in the Administration Building, room E one oh one.","我们每周五下午一点半到四点二十上课，地点是行政楼 E101。"],[51.66,60.72,12,"My office hours are Friday evening, six thirty to seven thirty, in Daoyuan Building, room five oh four A, and you can always email me.","我的答疑时间是周五晚上六点半到七点半，在道远楼 504A，也随时可以给我发邮件。"],[61.07,65.41,12,"TA office hours and all other details are on the course website.","助教的答疑时间和其他所有细节都在课程网站上。"],[65.76,68.2,12,"Office hours are there to be used.","答疑时间就是用来用的。"],[68.55,74.52,12,"Many students only show up the week before a deadline, so come early, even with half-formed questions.","很多同学只在截止前一周才来，请早点来，哪怕问题还没想清楚。"],[75.77,79.5,13,"Here's a small story about one of our previous TAs.","讲一个关于我们往届助教的小故事。"],[79.85,87.85,13,"He's considering starting a company in the direction of recursive self-improvement, or RSI for short.","他正在考虑在递归自我改进，也就是 RSI 方向创业。"],[88.2,93.16,13,"That means AI systems that help improve the next generation of AI systems.","也就是让 AI 系统去帮助改进下一代 AI 系统。"],[93.51,97.89,13,"I mention this because TAs in this course aren't just graders.","我提这个，是因为这门课的助教不只是改作业的人。"],[98.24,103.52,13,"They're active researchers, some going to top labs, some starting companies.","他们是活跃的研究者，有的去了顶尖实验室，有的在创业。"],[103.87,111.38,13,"And RSI is a theme I'll come back to at the very end of today, when I talk about where our group's research is heading.","RSI 这个主题我会在今天最后再谈到，那时我会讲我们组的研究方向。"],[112.63,114.81,14,"There are two channels you must join.","有两个渠道你必须加入。"],[115.16,123.65,14,"The official course website is where everything lives: the schedule, readings, slides, assignments and deadlines.","官方课程网站包含一切：课表、阅读材料、课件、作业和截止日期。"],[124.0,128.83,14,"On the left you can see the course description and the beginning of the schedule.","左边可以看到课程简介和课表的开头部分。"],[129.18,133.04,14,"Each week has recommended readings and a pre-lecture question.","每周都有推荐阅读和一个课前问题。"],[133.39,139.03,14,"Please glance at the pre-lecture question before each class; it'll make the lecture much easier to follow.","每次上课前请看一眼课前问题，这会让你更容易跟上课程。"],[139.38,145.23,14,"On the right is the WeChat group, which we'll use for quick announcements and discussion.","右边是微信群，我们用它发布通知和讨论。"],[145.58,148.99,14,"If you're enrolled, please scan the QR code to join.","如果你选了这门课，请扫码入群。"],[149.34,155.84,14,"These codes expire after a few days, so if it doesn't work, ask a classmate or a TA to add you.","二维码几天后会过期，如果扫不进去，请找同学或助教拉你进群。"],[157.09,161.36,15,"Let me set expectations clearly. This is an advanced graduate course.","我先把期望说清楚。这是一门高阶研究生课程。"],[161.71,170.47,15,"We'll go deep, and the goal is that by the end you can understand, design and actually implement NLP systems, not just talk about them.","我们会讲得很深，目标是到最后你能理解、设计并真正实现 NLP 系统，而不只是会谈论它们。"],[170.82,175.0,15,"I expect you to come to class regularly and join the discussion.","我希望大家按时上课，积极参与讨论。"],[175.35,180.75,15,"Now the prerequisites. Reports are written in LaTeX, and we'll give you a template.","再说先修要求。报告要用 LaTeX 写，我们会提供模板。"],[181.1,183.28,15,"Code should live on GitHub.","代码应该放在 GitHub 上。"],[183.63,187.6,15,"Assignments are in Python, using NumPy and PyTorch.","作业用 Python 完成，使用 NumPy 和 PyTorch。"],[187.95,195.91,15,"Machine learning background helps a lot, but if you don't have it you can still succeed; you'll just need to put in more effort early on.","机器学习基础会很有帮助，但没有也能学好，只是前期需要多花些功夫。"],[196.26,201.08,15,"So, a quick self-check: have you used LaTeX? GitHub? PyTorch?","那么快速自查一下：你用过 LaTeX 吗？GitHub 呢？PyTorch 呢？"],[201.43,207.24,15,"If you're missing any of these, the tutorial in the first weeks is made for you, and this is the moment to catch up.","如果有哪项还不会，开学头几周的辅导课就是为你准备的，现在正是补上的时候。"],[208.49,211.58,16,"Here's the tentative structure of the whole semester.","这是整个学期的暂定结构。"],[211.93,221.68,16,"We start with foundations: today's introduction, then linguistics and word embeddings, language models, and deep learning for NLP, meaning the Transformer and beyond.","我们从基础开始：今天的导论，然后是语言学与词嵌入、语言模型，以及 NLP 中的深度学习，也就是 Transformer 及其后续。"],[222.03,230.19,16,"Then we move to large language models themselves, and to RL for post-training, which is how they learn to align and to reason.","接着是大语言模型本身，以及用于后训练的强化学习，模型正是靠它学会对齐和推理。"],[230.54,237.57,16,"After that come LLM agents and harness engineering, which is about building the system around a model.","之后是大模型智能体和 harness 工程，也就是围绕模型搭建整个系统。"],[237.92,248.27,16,"Then a session on final projects and research sharing, medical LLMs, multimodal LLMs, efficiency, and finally applications and the future.","然后是期末项目介绍与研究分享、医疗大模型、多模态大模型、效率，最后是应用与未来。"],[248.62,256.13,16,"Notice the arc: from how a machine represents a single word, all the way to systems that reason, see and act.","注意这条主线：从机器如何表示一个单词，一直到能推理、能看、能行动的系统。"],[256.48,258.96,16,"Each lecture builds on the previous one.","每一讲都建立在前一讲的基础上。"],[259.31,264.02,16,"The exact order may shift a bit; the website always has the latest schedule.","具体顺序可能会有所调整，最新课表以网站为准。"],[265.27,268.07,17,"Let me be a bit provocative here.","这里我说得尖锐一点。"],[268.42,277.47,17,"The first four topics, the intro, linguistics and word embeddings, classic language models, and the Transformer, I've labeled too old.","前四个主题：导论、语言学与词嵌入、经典语言模型和 Transformer，我给它们贴上了“太老了”的标签。"],[277.82,284.28,17,"What I mean is that they're no longer the cutting edge. Nobody builds a product today with only word2vec.","我的意思是，它们已经不是前沿了。今天没人只用 word2vec 来做产品。"],[284.63,286.74,17,"But that doesn't mean we skip them.","但这并不意味着我们跳过它们。"],[287.09,294.52,17,"You can't really understand why an LLM works, or why it fails, without knowing where its ideas come from.","如果不知道大模型的思想从何而来，你就无法真正理解它为什么有效，或者为什么失败。"],[294.87,300.19,17,"Think of these as the grammar of the field: old, but you need them to read anything new.","把它们看作这个领域的语法：虽然老，但要读懂任何新东西都离不开它们。"],[300.54,305.57,17,"So we'll cover them efficiently, focusing on the intuitions that still matter today.","所以我们会高效地讲，重点放在今天依然重要的直觉上。"],[306.82,315.11,18,"The next block is the practical core: large language models, RL post-training, and LLM agents with the harness around them.","下一部分是实践核心：大语言模型、强化学习后训练，以及大模型智能体和围绕它的 harness。"],[315.46,317.52,18,"This is where you'll get hands-on.","这里就是你真正动手的地方。"],[317.87,324.9,18,"You'll learn how models are pretrained and post-trained, including supervised fine-tuning and reinforcement learning.","你会学习模型如何预训练和后训练，包括监督微调和强化学习。"],[325.25,331.02,18,"And you'll learn how to turn a model into an agent that calls tools and completes tasks.","你还会学习如何把模型变成能调用工具、完成任务的智能体。"],[331.37,337.66,18,"These are the skills companies are hiring for right now, and they map directly onto your assignments.","这些正是企业现在招聘所需的技能，也直接对应你们的作业。"],[338.01,343.41,18,"If you only remember one block of this course for your career, it will probably be this one.","如果这门课你只为职业发展记住一个部分，那很可能就是这一块。"],[344.66,349.54,19,"And here's my favorite line: final projects are all you need.","这是我最喜欢的一句话：期末项目就是你所需要的一切。"],[349.89,355.77,19,"Yes, it's a joke on the famous Attention Is All You Need paper, but I mean it seriously.","没错，这是在调侃著名的 Attention Is All You Need 论文，但我是认真的。"],[356.12,361.76,19,"The lecture on final projects and research sharing is a turning point in the semester.","期末项目介绍与研究分享这一讲，是整个学期的转折点。"],[362.11,367.27,19,"Everything before it gives you the tools; everything after it is what you do with them.","之前的内容给你工具，之后的内容是你用这些工具去做事。"],[367.62,373.8,19,"In my experience, students learn far more from one serious project than from any number of lectures.","根据我的经验，学生从一个认真做的项目里学到的，远远多于听再多的课。"],[374.15,381.38,19,"That's why the final project carries the biggest weight in your grade, and why I'll spend a good part of today talking about it.","这就是为什么期末项目在成绩中占比最大，也是为什么我今天会花不少时间来讲它。"],[382.63,391.73,20,"The last block is cutting-edge research: medical LLMs, multimodal LLMs, efficiency, and LLM applications and the future.","最后一部分是前沿研究：医疗大模型、多模态大模型、效率，以及大模型的应用与未来。"],[392.08,401.51,20,"These topics are moving so fast that some of what I teach may be updated between when I make the slides and when I give the lecture.","这些方向发展太快了，从我做课件到我上课之间，有些内容可能就已经更新了。"],[401.86,403.32,20,"That's part of the fun.","这也是乐趣所在。"],[403.67,411.18,20,"These lectures are also where many good final project ideas come from, because the open problems are right there.","很多好的期末项目点子也来自这几讲，因为开放问题就摆在那里。"],[411.53,420.1,20,"So the full picture is: a solid but quick foundation, a practical core, your own project, and then the research frontier.","所以整体图景是：扎实而快速的基础、实践核心、你自己的项目，然后是研究前沿。"],[421.35,423.18,21,"Now, how you'll be graded.","接下来讲怎么评分。"],[423.53,425.96,21,"Assignments are forty percent in total.","作业一共占百分之四十。"],[426.31,431.6,21,"Assignment one, on training word vectors, is worth ten percent.","作业一是训练词向量，占百分之十。"],[431.95,438.04,21,"Assignment two, on training a model with SFT and RLHF, is fifteen percent.","作业二是用 SFT 和 RLHF 训练模型，占百分之十五。"],[438.39,446.34,21,"And assignment three, on using APIs for prompt engineering and agents, is fifteen percent.","作业三是用 API 做提示工程和智能体，占百分之十五。"],[446.69,455.67,21,"Every assignment comes with a short report, plus code if there's coding, and we evaluate the reports with criteria similar to the final project.","每个作业都要交一份简短报告，涉及编程的还要附代码，报告的评价标准和期末项目类似。"],[456.02,460.2,21,"The final project is fifty-five percent, more than half your grade.","期末项目占百分之五十五，超过总成绩的一半。"],[460.55,464.86,21,"You'll write a report of at most six pages for the main body.","你要写一份报告，正文最多六页。"],[465.21,468.65,21,"Longer is not better, so please don't pad it.","写得长并不更好，请不要凑篇幅。"],[469.0,470.91,21,"You'll also present a poster.","你还要做一次海报展示。"],[471.26,478.12,21,"Participation, meaning quizzes, guest lectures and the course evaluation, is the remaining five percent.","课堂参与，包括小测、嘉宾讲座和课程评估，占剩下的百分之五。"],[478.47,483.79,21,"The message from these numbers is clear: plan your semester around the project.","这些数字传达的信息很清楚：围绕项目来规划你的学期。"]]},{"n":3,"title":"Three Assignments and the Final Project","blurb":"The three hands-on assignments, from word vectors through SFT and RLHF to prompting and agents, then the final project: proposals, team size, posters, reports and assessment.","file":"lecture01_part3.mp4","poster":"lecture01_part3.jpg","duration":682.5,"first":22,"last":36,"slides":[{"n":22,"title":"Assignments 1: Training word vector.","t":0.8},{"n":23,"title":"Assignments 2: Training NLP model with SFT and RLHF","t":50.53},{"n":24,"title":"Assignment 3: Using API for Prompt Engineering and LLM Agents","t":101.51},{"n":25,"title":"Example of Poster","t":154.92},{"n":26,"title":"Report for the final project","t":198.43},{"n":27,"title":"Students complete a research project in teams of 1-3 [Optional] Draft proposal deadline: Nov. 13th 11:59pm (simply expla","t":233.69},{"n":28,"title":"Slide 28","t":289.23},{"n":29,"title":"What can we do for the final project?","t":329.99},{"n":30,"title":"Philosophy : select one of given proposals (you could do nothing but wait for the release of proposals). OR submit a cus","t":360.33},{"n":31,"title":"Typical projects (we will release a detailed list later): Fine-tune (or RL) a language model (e.g., Qwen) yourself for a","t":414.86},{"n":32,"title":"Report of final project might be publicly released, otherwise please specify reasons. released in our website released i","t":478.18},{"n":33,"title":"Example: ArXiv+HF+Github","t":521.05},{"n":34,"title":"Team size: Students may do final projects sololy, or in teams of up to 3 people. Please specify reasons to do project wi","t":555.87},{"n":35,"title":"Final project assessment","t":606.35},{"n":36,"title":"Submission Deadlines ACL ARR (four times per year) October 12 Feb. ACL,SIGIR, ICML March, COLM 2026 (https://colmweb.org","t":637.89}],"sents":[[0.8,7.91,22,"Let's look at each assignment briefly. The first one is about training word vectors.","我们简单看看每个作业。第一个是训练词向量。"],[8.26,14.18,22,"The left figure shows the core idea: each word becomes a point in a vector space.","左图展示了核心思想：每个词都变成向量空间中的一个点。"],[14.53,21.03,22,"Words with related meanings end up close together, and directions can carry meaning.","意思相关的词会靠得很近，而方向本身也能承载含义。"],[21.38,25.35,22,"On the right are the two classic word2vec training setups.","右边是 word2vec 的两种经典训练方式。"],[25.7,29.76,22,"CBOW predicts a word from its surrounding context.","CBOW 用周围的上下文来预测一个词。"],[30.11,35.48,22,"Skip-gram does the reverse, and predicts the context from a word.","Skip-gram 则反过来，用一个词去预测它的上下文。"],[35.83,44.68,22,"This assignment is small, but it gives you a real feel for how a machine can learn meaning purely from co-occurrence statistics.","这个作业不大，但能让你真切体会到机器如何仅凭共现统计就学到含义。"],[45.03,49.13,22,"We'll cover the theory in the next lecture, so you'll be well prepared.","下一讲我们会讲相关理论，所以你会有充分准备。"],[50.38,55.21,23,"Assignment two takes a big step up: you'll actually train a language model.","作业二难度大幅提升：你要真正训练一个语言模型。"],[55.56,60.55,23,"First with supervised fine-tuning, then with reinforcement learning from feedback.","先做监督微调，再做基于反馈的强化学习。"],[60.9,65.82,23,"For fine-tuning, you can use LLMFactory, a toolkit from our group.","微调部分可以用 LLMFactory，这是我们组开发的工具包。"],[66.17,69.66,23,"The code on the slide shows how simple the workflow is.","幻灯片上的代码展示了整个流程有多简单。"],[70.01,77.08,23,"Pick a backbone model, prepare the data, train, and deploy it on the command line or with a Gradio demo.","选一个基座模型，准备数据，训练，然后在命令行或用 Gradio 演示部署。"],[77.43,86.73,23,"For the RL part, we point you to verl, an open-source reinforcement learning framework widely used for LLM post-training.","强化学习部分，我们推荐 verl，一个广泛用于大模型后训练的开源强化学习框架。"],[87.08,90.41,23,"The goal isn't to beat state-of-the-art models.","目标不是打败最先进的模型。"],[90.76,100.11,23,"It's to go through the full pipeline once yourself, so that when we talk about SFT and RLHF in lectures, you know what it actually feels like.","而是让你亲自走一遍完整流程，这样课上讲 SFT 和 RLHF 时，你知道它实际是什么感觉。"],[101.36,107.16,24,"Assignment three is about using LLMs through APIs: prompt engineering and agents.","作业三是通过 API 使用大模型：提示工程和智能体。"],[107.51,110.8,24,"The figure shows a typical multi-agent setup.","这张图展示了一个典型的多智能体架构。"],[111.15,120.12,24,"A commander agent receives the user's question, a writer agent produces code or answers, and a safeguard agent checks them.","指挥智能体接收用户问题，写作智能体生成代码或答案，安全守卫智能体负责检查。"],[120.47,124.82,24,"They loop until the question is answered, or time runs out.","它们循环往复，直到问题被回答或超时为止。"],[125.17,131.26,24,"This pattern of several roles cooperating is very common in real agent systems.","多个角色协作的这种模式，在真实的智能体系统中非常常见。"],[131.61,138.47,24,"For APIs, you can use providers like SiliconFlow or OpenRouter, which give you access to many models cheaply.","API 方面，可以用硅基流动或 OpenRouter 这样的服务商，便宜地调用很多模型。"],[138.82,144.55,24,"For agent frameworks, there are options like CAMEL, Dify, LangChain and Coze.","智能体框架方面，可以选 CAMEL、Dify、LangChain 和 Coze 等。"],[144.9,151.19,24,"You'll submit a report with code, showing that you can make an agent do something genuinely useful.","你要提交一份带代码的报告，展示你能让智能体做出真正有用的事。"],[151.54,153.52,24,"More details will come later.","更多细节之后公布。"],[154.77,160.87,25,"Now, the final project. Part of it is a poster presentation, so here's what a poster looks like.","现在讲期末项目。其中一部分是海报展示，先看看海报长什么样。"],[161.22,167.14,25,"On the left is a poster from a previous LLM course here at CUHK-Shenzhen.","左边是港中深往届大模型课程的一张海报。"],[167.49,175.94,25,"Notice the structure: introduction, motivation, method and results, all on one page, with figures doing most of the talking.","注意它的结构：引言、动机、方法和结果，全在一页上，主要靠图来说话。"],[176.29,180.96,25,"On the right, you see what a poster session at a big conference looks like.","右边是大型学术会议上海报环节的样子。"],[181.31,187.28,25,"Crowded halls, people walking around, and you have about a minute to catch someone's interest.","大厅里人头攒动，大家走来走去，你只有大约一分钟去吸引别人的兴趣。"],[187.63,190.91,25,"A good poster is not your paper shrunk down.","好的海报不是把论文缩小。"],[191.26,197.03,25,"It's a visual story: one clear question, one key figure, one main result.","它是一个视觉故事：一个清晰的问题、一张关键的图、一个主要的结果。"],[198.28,203.44,26,"The report for the final project should look like a real research paper.","期末项目报告应该像一篇真正的研究论文。"],[203.79,211.06,26,"Here I'm showing the first page of Attention Is All You Need, the Transformer paper, which we'll study in a few weeks.","这里展示的是 Attention Is All You Need 的第一页，也就是 Transformer 论文，几周后我们会学到。"],[211.41,219.62,26,"Notice the clear title and authors, and a concise abstract that says what problem, what method and what result.","注意它清晰的标题和作者，以及简洁的摘要：说明了什么问题、什么方法、什么结果。"],[219.97,221.35,26,"Then comes the body.","然后才是正文。"],[221.7,226.57,26,"That's the standard we're aiming for: write it like you would submit it to a conference.","这就是我们追求的标准：按投会议的标准来写。"],[226.92,232.29,26,"We'll give you a LaTeX template, and remember, at most six pages for the main body.","我们会提供 LaTeX 模板，记住，正文最多六页。"],[233.54,236.54,27,"Here's the timeline structure for the final project.","这是期末项目的时间安排。"],[236.89,239.58,27,"You'll work in teams of one to three.","你们以一到三人为一组完成。"],[239.93,249.59,27,"There's an optional draft proposal, due November thirteenth at eleven fifty-nine pm, where you simply explain your idea in one page.","有一个可选的提案草稿，截止时间是 11 月 13 日晚 11:59，只需用一页纸说明你的想法。"],[249.94,256.8,27,"Then there's the poster session on December eighteenth, where the TAs and I can give you suggestions for revision.","然后是 12 月 18 日的海报展示，助教和我会在现场给你修改建议。"],[257.15,262.84,27,"The final poster itself is due the day before, December seventeenth, at five pm.","海报本身要在前一天，也就是 12 月 17 日下午五点前提交。"],[263.19,271.1,27,"And the final paper is due December twenty-fifth, so you can still improve the report after getting feedback at the poster session.","最终论文 12 月 25 日截止，这样你在海报环节拿到反馈后，还能继续改进报告。"],[271.45,277.75,27,"The course website is always the authoritative source for dates; that's the schedule we'll actually follow.","日期一律以课程网站为准，我们实际按那个时间表执行。"],[278.1,281.92,27,"The one thing to remember is at the bottom: start early.","要记住的就是最下面这句：尽早开始。"],[282.27,287.83,27,"The deadlines fall near exam weeks, and every year the teams that start late regret it.","截止日期临近考试周，每年开始晚的小组都会后悔。"],[289.08,292.33,28,"This is the full semester schedule from the course website.","这是课程网站上的完整学期课表。"],[292.68,296.5,28,"You don't need to read it now, but let me point out the rhythm.","现在不需要细看，但我来指出它的节奏。"],[296.85,306.68,28,"Each row is a week: the lecture topic, recommended readings, a pre-lecture question, slides, coding resources, and deadlines in the last column.","每一行是一周：课程主题、推荐阅读、课前问题、课件、编程资源，最后一列是截止日期。"],[307.03,312.4,28,"The green rows are tutorials, where the TAs walk you through practical tools.","绿色的行是辅导课，助教会带大家上手实用工具。"],[312.75,317.49,28,"Look at the right-hand column, and you'll see assignments coming out and falling due.","看最右边一列，你会看到作业的发布和截止。"],[317.84,322.27,28,"Near the end come the poster and final report deadlines.","接近学期末是海报和最终报告的截止日期。"],[322.62,328.59,28,"Please bookmark this page and check it every week. It's the single source of truth for dates.","请收藏这个页面，每周查看。它是日期的唯一权威来源。"],[329.84,334.67,29,"Before we talk about what you can do for the final project, a warning.","在讲期末项目可以做什么之前，先提个醒。"],[335.02,340.58,29,"The workload is genuinely high. This is not a project you can finish in the last weekend.","工作量真的很大。这不是最后一个周末就能赶完的项目。"],[340.93,348.28,29,"If you're taking several heavy courses this semester, or working part-time, think carefully about how much time you have.","如果你这学期还修了好几门重课，或者在兼职，请认真想想自己有多少时间。"],[348.63,354.51,29,"Maybe choose a smaller, well-defined project rather than an ambitious one you can't finish.","也许应该选一个小而明确的项目，而不是一个做不完的宏大项目。"],[354.86,358.93,29,"And the bold line says it all: prepare as early as possible.","加粗的那句话说明了一切：尽早准备。"],[360.18,362.53,30,"There are two ways to get a project.","获得项目有两种方式。"],[362.88,368.41,30,"You can pick one of the proposals we release; you can even simply wait for that list.","你可以从我们发布的选题中选一个，甚至可以直接等名单公布。"],[368.76,373.26,30,"Or you can propose your own custom project, which needs our approval.","或者你可以提出自己的定制项目，但需要我们批准。"],[373.61,380.56,30,"We also run an optional call for project proposals, with the deadline tentatively on November thirteenth.","我们还有一个可选的项目提案征集，截止日期暂定 11 月 13 日。"],[380.91,385.21,30,"Interestingly, proposals don't have to come only from students.","有意思的是，提案不一定只来自学生。"],[385.56,396.0,30,"They can come from researchers or engineers in companies, from PhD students and RAs in our group, or from faculty members, for example your own supervisor.","也可以来自企业的研究员或工程师、我们组的博士生和研究助理，或者教师，比如你自己的导师。"],[396.35,401.75,30,"Basically, anyone with a good problem is welcome, though we reserve the right to say no.","基本上，任何有好问题的人都欢迎，不过我们保留拒绝的权利。"],[402.1,409.9,30,"So if your lab, your company, or a friend has a real problem that needs NLP, that can become your project.","所以如果你的实验室、公司或朋友有需要 NLP 的真实问题，它就可以成为你的项目。"],[410.25,413.46,30,"Real problems usually make the best projects.","真实问题往往能做出最好的项目。"],[414.71,418.4,31,"What do typical projects look like? Here are some categories.","典型的项目是什么样的？这里列了几类。"],[418.75,424.84,31,"You could fine-tune or do RL on an open model like Qwen, for a problem you care about.","你可以针对自己关心的问题，对 Qwen 这样的开源模型做微调或强化学习。"],[425.19,430.72,31,"And you could actually ask whether tuning is even necessary, compared with good prompting.","甚至可以研究：和好的提示相比，微调到底有没有必要。"],[431.07,438.01,31,"You could evaluate existing frontier LLMs to understand their capabilities, limitations and risks.","你可以评测现有的前沿大模型，了解它们的能力、局限和风险。"],[438.36,443.89,31,"You could build an agent system for math, finance, medicine or law.","你可以为数学、金融、医疗或法律搭建一个智能体系统。"],[444.24,450.45,31,"Or you could build an app that uses AI, or was even built with AI.","或者做一个使用 AI 的应用，甚至是用 AI 开发出来的应用。"],[450.8,458.23,31,"A research paper involving NLP is also fine, and new this year, you can join a competition and write a technical report.","一篇涉及 NLP 的研究论文也可以；今年新增的是，你可以参加一个比赛并写技术报告。"],[458.58,464.55,31,"Notice that a survey is crossed out on the list, so please don't plan on a pure survey.","注意列表里“综述”被划掉了，所以请不要打算只写一篇综述。"],[464.9,473.95,31,"And note the red line on the right: if we really like your proposal, you might get compute to train a model with more than ten billion parameters.","再看右边的红字：如果我们非常喜欢你的提案，你可能获得算力去训练百亿参数以上的模型。"],[474.3,476.78,31,"So ambition can pay off.","所以，有野心是会有回报的。"],[478.03,482.34,32,"We strongly encourage you to make your final project public.","我们强烈鼓励大家把期末项目公开。"],[482.69,486.75,32,"Good reports may be posted on our course website.","优秀的报告可能会发布在我们的课程网站上。"],[487.1,494.45,32,"If the quality is high, put it on arXiv, but please don't post low-quality preprints there.","如果质量高，可以发到 arXiv 上，但请不要把低质量的预印本放上去。"],[494.8,499.22,32,"If you're unsure, ask your supervisor or the teaching team.","如果拿不准，可以问你的导师或教学团队。"],[499.57,503.1,32,"Keep your code on GitHub, and link it in the report.","代码放在 GitHub 上，并在报告里附上链接。"],[503.45,508.85,32,"If you train a model, upload it to Hugging Face, where you can even serve a demo.","如果你训练了模型，就上传到 Hugging Face，甚至可以在那里部署演示。"],[509.2,514.52,32,"Here's a concrete goal I like: aim for over one hundred stars on your GitHub repo.","我喜欢的一个具体目标是：让你的 GitHub 仓库获得一百颗星以上。"],[514.87,519.65,32,"That means people actually found your work useful, and it looks great on a CV.","这说明别人真的觉得你的工作有用，写在简历上也很亮眼。"],[520.9,524.64,33,"Here's an example of what doing it right looks like.","这是一个做得好的例子。"],[524.99,531.25,33,"The paper is on arXiv, the code is on GitHub, and the dataset is on Hugging Face, all linked together.","论文在 arXiv 上，代码在 GitHub 上，数据集在 Hugging Face 上，三者互相链接。"],[531.6,536.26,33,"See how the paper itself links straight to the code repository.","看，论文本身就直接链接到了代码仓库。"],[536.61,544.57,33,"When someone reads your paper and immediately finds working code and a downloadable model, your work gets used and cited.","当别人读你的论文时，马上就能找到能跑的代码和可下载的模型，你的工作就会被使用和引用。"],[544.92,549.94,33,"Projects that only exist as a PDF are usually forgotten quickly.","只以 PDF 形式存在的项目，通常很快就会被遗忘。"],[550.29,554.47,33,"So from day one, plan to release all three pieces.","所以从第一天起，就计划好发布这三样东西。"],[555.72,557.71,34,"Now some rules on teamwork.","接下来是关于团队合作的一些规则。"],[558.06,561.59,34,"You can work alone or in teams of up to three.","你可以单独完成，也可以最多三人组队。"],[561.94,566.28,34,"If you want a larger team, you need to justify it, and we may say no.","如果想组更大的队，需要说明理由，我们也可能拒绝。"],[566.63,575.12,34,"We do recommend teams, but a bigger team is expected to do a bigger project, and every member should contribute substantially.","我们推荐组队，但人越多，项目就应该越大，而且每个成员都要有实质性贡献。"],[575.47,579.57,34,"In the final report, you'll state what each member contributed.","在最终报告里，你们要写明每个成员的贡献。"],[579.92,588.81,34,"If contributions are clearly unequal, grades may be differentiated, and you can always contact us confidentially if there's a problem.","如果贡献明显不均，成绩可能会有所区分；有问题也可以随时私下联系我们。"],[589.16,593.94,34,"External collaborators are fine, but be clear about which parts are yours.","可以有外部合作者，但要说清楚哪些部分是你做的。"],[594.29,599.45,34,"Every custom project gets a mentor, either external or someone from our team.","每个定制项目都会有一位导师，可以是外部的，也可以是我们团队的人。"],[599.8,604.95,34,"For compute, we'll use Kaggle resources, and we'll share details later.","算力方面，我们会使用 Kaggle 的资源，细节之后公布。"],[606.2,608.59,35,"How is the final project assessed?","期末项目怎么评估？"],[608.94,615.53,35,"The report is worth forty-five percent of your course grade, and is reviewed by the TAs.","报告占课程总成绩的百分之四十五，由助教评审。"],[615.88,620.66,35,"The poster presentation is worth ten percent, reviewed by the TAs and me.","海报展示占百分之十，由助教和我评审。"],[621.01,625.56,35,"At the poster session, you'll also review each other's posters.","在海报环节，你们还会互相评审彼此的海报。"],[625.91,632.77,35,"That cross-review doesn't count toward your grade, but it's a great way to learn how to give and receive research feedback.","互评不计入成绩，但它是学习如何给出和接受研究反馈的好机会。"],[633.12,636.49,35,"And that's a skill you'll need in any career.","这是在任何职业中都需要的技能。"],[637.74,642.05,36,"If your project turns out well, why stop at a grade? Submit it to a real conference.","如果你的项目做得好，何必止步于一个分数？把它投到真正的学术会议去。"],[642.4,644.87,36,"The slide lists the main venues.","幻灯片列出了主要的会议。"],[645.22,652.61,36,"ACL Rolling Review accepts submissions four times a year, and feeds into the major NLP conferences.","ACL Rolling Review 每年接收四次投稿，对接各大 NLP 会议。"],[652.96,657.03,36,"Around February there are venues like ACL, SIGIR and ICML.","二月前后有 ACL、SIGIR 和 ICML 等会议。"],[657.38,664.16,36,"Around March there's COLM, the conference dedicated to language modeling, and around May there's NeurIPS.","三月前后有专注语言建模的 COLM，五月前后有 NeurIPS。"],[664.51,667.6,36,"Always check the official sites for exact deadlines.","具体截止日期请务必查看官方网站。"],[667.95,674.89,36,"The TAs may help if they're interested in your topic, and they might connect you with other students in our group.","如果助教对你的题目感兴趣，可能会帮忙，也可能把你介绍给我们组的其他同学。"],[675.24,680.6,36,"You can also work with external collaborators; just please follow academic ethics.","你也可以和外部人员合作，但请遵守学术道德。"]]},{"n":4,"title":"Finding Good Ideas and Succeeding in This Course","blurb":"Where good project ideas come from, including startups such as FriesAI, how the course itself was designed, what it covers and leaves out, and how to succeed rather than fail.","file":"lecture01_part4.mp4","poster":"lecture01_part4.jpg","duration":693.4,"first":37,"last":53,"slides":[{"n":37,"title":"How to better prepare a final project in NLP?","t":0.8},{"n":38,"title":"Ideas from where?","t":47.87},{"n":39,"title":"Ideas from where?","t":94.26},{"n":40,"title":"For startups: FriesAI for classroom learning","t":134.22},{"n":41,"title":"截至2025年4月12日13点30分，薯塔AI已覆盖港中深60%的本科生，港中深注册人数达3579人，总注册人数达4680人。其中日活跃用户为1239人，平均每日AI问答数2898条。薯塔AI目前正在逐步推广至其他七所中外合办院校，进一步提","t":182.99},{"n":42,"title":"For startups","t":232.77},{"n":43,"title":"Define the learning objectives:","t":277.32},{"n":44,"title":"Select appropriate resources:","t":329.27},{"n":45,"title":"Design engaging lectures:","t":373.99},{"n":46,"title":"Provide hands-on practice:","t":404.46},{"n":47,"title":"Foster collaboration and discussion:","t":451.21},{"n":48,"title":"Seek feedback and iterate this course:","t":479.01},{"n":49,"title":"What is in our course","t":502.3},{"n":50,"title":"What is not in our course","t":535.98},{"n":51,"title":"How not to fail in this course","t":572.9},{"n":52,"title":"How to success in this course","t":606.72},{"n":53,"title":"You might obtain from a great project","t":645.01}],"sents":[[0.8,4.62,37,"So how do you come up with a good final project?","那么，怎样想出一个好的期末项目？"],[4.97,10.09,37,"Well, you could ask ChatGPT, and that's literally what this screenshot shows.","你可以问 ChatGPT，这张截图就是这么做的。"],[10.44,17.06,37,"Someone asks for project ideas for an NLP course focused on large language models.","有人在问：一门侧重大语言模型的 NLP 课程，期末项目可以做什么。"],[17.41,30.25,37,"The answer is reasonable: fine-tuning for a specific task, bias analysis, zero-shot learning, multimodal models, LMs as knowledge bases, interactive fiction.","回答还算合理：针对特定任务微调、偏见分析、零样本学习、多模态模型、语言模型作为知识库、互动小说。"],[30.6,36.19,37,"But notice how generic it is. Hundreds of other students will get the same list.","但注意它有多泛泛。成百上千的学生都会得到同样的列表。"],[36.54,44.62,37,"An LLM is a fine brainstorming partner, but the best ideas usually come from somewhere more personal.","大模型是不错的头脑风暴伙伴，但最好的点子通常来自更个人化的地方。"],[44.97,46.47,37,"Let's look at where.","我们来看看是哪里。"],[47.72,51.54,38,"The first source of ideas is the research literature.","点子的第一个来源是研究文献。"],[51.89,58.51,38,"For NLP, the ACL Anthology has essentially every paper from the main NLP conferences.","NLP 方面，ACL Anthology 基本收录了主要 NLP 会议的所有论文。"],[58.86,66.86,38,"For machine learning, OpenReview lets you browse ICLR submissions, often with the reviews, which are a great education in themselves.","机器学习方面，可以在 OpenReview 上浏览 ICLR 的投稿，往往还附有审稿意见，这本身就是很好的学习材料。"],[67.21,72.2,38,"For LLM-specific work, look at the accepted papers of COLM.","大模型方向的工作，可以看 COLM 的录用论文。"],[72.55,77.79,38,"And for human-computer interaction, there are the HCI venues listed here.","人机交互方面，这里列出了 HCI 的相关会议。"],[78.14,86.14,38,"I'd especially encourage you to look at the intersection on the bottom line: NLP plus LLMs plus HCI.","我特别鼓励大家关注最下面这行的交叉领域：NLP 加大模型加人机交互。"],[86.49,92.86,38,"How people actually interact with these models is a very rich, and still underexplored, area.","人们究竟如何与这些模型交互，是一个非常丰富而且仍未被充分探索的领域。"],[94.11,96.58,39,"The second source of ideas is you.","点子的第二个来源是你自己。"],[96.93,99.16,39,"Your previous major is an asset.","你之前的专业是一笔财富。"],[99.51,106.58,39,"If you studied finance, management or social science, you know problems that pure computer scientists don't.","如果你学过金融、管理或社会科学，你就了解纯计算机背景的人不知道的问题。"],[106.93,111.0,39,"Your personal interests count too, and I'll show you a nice example in a minute.","个人兴趣也很重要，待会儿我会给大家看一个很好的例子。"],[111.35,116.01,39,"Look at the resources around you: does a friend or a lab have unique data?","看看你身边的资源：有没有朋友或实验室拥有独特的数据？"],[116.36,120.14,39,"Data is often the scarcest ingredient in NLP.","在 NLP 里，数据往往是最稀缺的要素。"],[120.49,125.77,39,"And think about existing use cases: where are the real users, and how could you reach them?","再想想现有的使用场景：真实用户在哪里，你怎样触达他们？"],[126.12,132.82,39,"A project that combines AI with something you know deeply is much harder for others to copy.","把 AI 和你深入了解的领域结合起来的项目，别人很难复制。"],[134.07,140.61,40,"For some of you, a project can even turn into a startup. Here's a real example supported by our group.","对有些同学来说，项目甚至可以变成创业。这是我们组支持的一个真实例子。"],[140.96,150.79,40,"This is FriesAI, or Shuta AI in Chinese, an AI learning assistant for courses at Sino-foreign universities and international schools.","这是薯塔AI，一款面向中外合作院校和国际学校课程的 AI 学习助手。"],[151.14,159.71,40,"Students share course slides, ask the AI questions about them, search across documents, get automatic summaries and translations, and so on.","学生可以共享课件、就课件向 AI 提问、跨文档检索、自动生成摘要和翻译等等。"],[160.06,170.09,40,"The student team behind it has passed two thousand monthly active users, and serves a large share of the courses at CUHK-Shenzhen.","背后的学生团队已获得超过两千月活用户，服务港中深的大部分课程。"],[170.44,173.56,40,"They're also expanding to other universities.","他们还在向其他高校拓展。"],[173.91,181.59,40,"The key insight: they started from a pain point they personally had as students, and solved it with LLMs.","关键在于：他们从自己作为学生的亲身痛点出发，用大模型解决了它。"],[182.84,185.52,41,"Here's some more detail on how far it has gone.","再看看它已经走了多远。"],[185.87,194.36,41,"According to the numbers on this slide from April twenty twenty-five, it covered about sixty percent of undergraduates at CUHK-Shenzhen.","根据幻灯片上 2025 年 4 月的数据，它覆盖了港中深约百分之六十的本科生。"],[194.71,203.4,41,"There were over three and a half thousand registered users here, and close to four thousand seven hundred in total.","港中深注册用户超过三千五百人，总注册人数接近四千七百人。"],[203.75,209.67,41,"More than a thousand users were active daily, asking nearly three thousand AI questions per day.","日活跃用户超过一千人，平均每天有近三千条 AI 问答。"],[210.02,214.69,41,"It was also being rolled out to seven other Sino-foreign universities.","它还在逐步推广到其他七所中外合办院校。"],[215.04,221.62,41,"You can see the interface: courses organized by semester, each with its own slides and AI assistant.","你可以看到界面：课程按学期组织，每门课都有自己的课件和 AI 助手。"],[221.97,224.56,41,"Some of you may already be users.","你们中有些人可能已经是用户了。"],[224.91,231.37,41,"It shows that a student project, done well and close to real users, can have real impact.","这说明一个学生项目，只要做得好、贴近真实用户，就能产生真正的影响。"],[232.62,237.17,42,"Here's another example, and it's a nice one because it comes from a hobby.","再看一个例子，它很棒，因为它源自一个爱好。"],[237.52,240.68,42,"A student, Zhu Yuxuan, loves tennis.","朱宇轩同学热爱网球。"],[241.03,251.35,42,"He combined it with AI and built an app called TennSync, Wangshi in Chinese, which automatically edits your tennis videos into highlight clips.","他把网球和 AI 结合，开发了一款叫“网事” TennSync 的应用，能自动把网球视频剪成集锦。"],[251.7,256.98,42,"Recording a match is easy; cutting the good rallies out of an hour of video is painful.","录一场比赛很容易，但从一小时的视频里剪出精彩回合却很痛苦。"],[257.33,259.44,42,"His app does it in seconds.","他的应用几秒钟就能搞定。"],[259.79,267.39,42,"According to the slide, it has served over a thousand users and saved tennis players more than five thousand hours.","根据幻灯片，它已服务一千多名用户，为网球爱好者节省了超过五千小时。"],[267.74,271.56,42,"That's the power of combining a personal interest with AI.","这就是把个人兴趣与 AI 结合的力量。"],[271.91,275.92,42,"So, what do you love doing, and what's annoying about it?","那么，你热爱做什么？其中又有什么让你烦恼的地方？"],[277.17,283.63,43,"Let me step back and explain how I designed this course, starting with the learning objectives, in three layers.","我退一步讲讲我是如何设计这门课的，先从学习目标说起，分三个层次。"],[283.98,288.93,43,"Knowledge: you should understand the basic concepts and principles of NLP.","知识：你应该理解 NLP 的基本概念和原理。"],[289.28,299.27,43,"You should be able to use it effectively in study, work and research, and, importantly, know which problems NLP is good at and which it isn't.","能在学习、工作和研究中有效使用它，而且很重要的是，知道哪些问题适合用 NLP 解决，哪些不适合。"],[299.62,308.07,43,"Skills: you should be able to train an NLP model through a complete pipeline, and call LLM APIs in your daily work.","技能：你应该能按完整流程训练一个 NLP 模型，并在日常工作中调用大模型 API。"],[308.42,316.75,43,"Values and attitude: appreciate the importance of data, and get used to a data-driven way of solving problems.","价值观与态度：认识到数据的重要性，习惯用数据驱动的方式解决问题。"],[317.1,322.12,43,"And stay aware of the limitations and risks of tools like ChatGPT.","同时清楚 ChatGPT 这类工具的局限和风险。"],[322.47,327.87,43,"That last one matters. Being a good user of AI means knowing when not to trust it.","最后这点很重要。善用 AI，意味着知道什么时候不该相信它。"],[329.12,336.63,44,"Next, resources. In a field this fast, textbooks are always behind, so we learn from live sources.","接下来是资源。在这样快速发展的领域，教科书总是落后，所以我们从实时的来源学习。"],[336.98,341.08,44,"Recent arXiv papers, which people share daily on social media.","最新的 arXiv 论文，大家每天都在社交媒体上分享。"],[341.43,344.72,44,"GitHub, where popularity really does mean something.","GitHub，在那里受欢迎程度确实很说明问题。"],[345.07,352.54,44,"Hugging Face, for new models and datasets, plus its daily papers page, which is a great way to see what's hot.","Hugging Face，用来找新模型和数据集，它的每日论文页面也是了解热点的好去处。"],[352.89,364.79,44,"And blogs from OpenAI and from individual researchers like Lilian Weng, Yao Fu and Jianlin Su, which often explain ideas more clearly than the papers do.","还有 OpenAI 的博客，以及翁荔、符尧、苏剑林等研究者的个人博客，它们往往比论文讲得更清楚。"],[365.14,369.08,44,"Get into the habit of spending ten minutes a day skimming one of these.","养成每天花十分钟浏览其中一个的习惯。"],[369.43,372.59,44,"Over a semester, that adds up enormously.","一个学期下来，积累会非常可观。"],[373.84,378.39,45,"I also want the lectures to be engaging, not just me talking for three hours.","我也希望课堂是互动的，而不是我一个人讲三个小时。"],[378.74,383.52,45,"We'll have discussions at the end of lectures, and in-class presentations.","我们会在课程结尾安排讨论，还有课堂展示。"],[383.87,392.16,45,"In class, please interrupt me whenever you have a question; if you're confused, others probably are too.","上课时有问题请随时打断我；如果你困惑，别人很可能也一样。"],[392.51,395.47,45,"Finally, make friends with me and the TAs.","最后，和我以及助教们交朋友。"],[395.82,403.06,45,"Many research opportunities, recommendations and collaborations start with a simple conversation after class.","很多科研机会、推荐和合作，都始于课后的一次简单交谈。"],[404.31,409.59,46,"Hands-on practice is essential. You can't learn to train models by watching slides.","动手实践至关重要。光看课件是学不会训练模型的。"],[409.94,414.61,46,"Besides our own repositories, here are some excellent learning projects.","除了我们自己的仓库，这里还有一些很好的学习项目。"],[414.96,424.5,46,"Andrej Karpathy's nanoGPT and minGPT are tiny, readable GPT implementations; you can read the whole thing in an afternoon.","Andrej Karpathy 的 nanoGPT 和 minGPT 是小巧易读的 GPT 实现，一个下午就能读完。"],[424.85,428.67,46,"Llama two dot c runs a Llama-style model in plain C.","llama2.c 用纯 C 语言运行 Llama 风格的模型。"],[429.02,432.11,46,"TinyLlama shows how a small model is pretrained.","TinyLlama 展示了小模型是如何预训练的。"],[432.46,438.75,46,"From our group, there's HuatuoGPT, LLMZoo and LLMFactory.","我们组的有 HuatuoGPT、LLMZoo 和 LLMFactory。"],[439.1,446.17,46,"My suggestion: pick one of the small GPT repos and actually train it on a small dataset during the first month.","我的建议是：选一个小型 GPT 仓库，在第一个月里真正用一个小数据集把它训练起来。"],[446.52,449.81,46,"It will make the lectures on language models and Transformers click.","这会让你在学习语言模型和 Transformer 的课时豁然开朗。"],[451.06,453.2,47,"On collaboration and ownership.","关于合作和归属。"],[453.55,462.73,47,"You own the copyright of your project, unless our teaching team made a substantial contribution, in which case please acknowledge us.","项目的版权归你所有，除非我们教学团队做出了实质性贡献，那种情况下请致谢我们。"],[463.08,466.52,47,"You're very welcome to discuss your ideas with the teaching team.","非常欢迎你和教学团队讨论你的想法。"],[466.87,471.9,47,"And we encourage you to discuss and collaborate with each other.","我们也鼓励同学之间互相讨论、合作。"],[472.25,477.61,47,"Some of the best ideas come from two people with different backgrounds talking over coffee.","一些最好的点子，来自两个不同背景的人边喝咖啡边聊天。"],[478.86,486.61,48,"This course is a living thing. Every year we rebuild a large part of it, because the field changes so fast.","这门课是活的。每年我们都会重建其中很大一部分，因为这个领域变化太快了。"],[486.96,490.08,48,"So please tell us when something works and when it doesn't.","所以请告诉我们哪些有效、哪些无效。"],[490.43,497.41,48,"If a lecture was too fast, if an assignment was unclear, or if you think we should cover a new topic, let us know.","如果某节课太快、某个作业不清楚，或者你觉得我们该讲某个新主题，请告诉我们。"],[497.76,500.9,48,"Your feedback directly shapes the next version of the course.","你的反馈会直接影响这门课的下一个版本。"],[502.15,504.58,49,"To summarize what's in this course.","总结一下这门课包含什么。"],[504.93,511.65,49,"The very basics of NLP, with the honest caveat that many older techniques aren't that practical anymore.","NLP 最基础的内容，不过坦白说，很多老技术现在已经没那么实用了。"],[512.0,515.92,49,"Large language models, including training and what comes after.","大语言模型，包括训练以及训练之后的内容。"],[516.27,521.49,49,"Data engineering, because data quality often matters more than model architecture.","数据工程，因为数据质量往往比模型架构更重要。"],[521.84,524.98,49,"Prompt engineering, and real NLP applications.","提示工程，以及真实的 NLP 应用。"],[525.33,527.65,49,"And finally, where the field is heading.","最后，是这个领域的未来走向。"],[528.0,534.58,49,"That last one is a moving target, so expect some lectures to feel a bit like news reports from the frontier.","最后这一项是个移动的靶子，所以有些课会有点像来自前沿的新闻播报。"],[535.83,539.3,50,"It's equally important to say what's not in this course.","同样重要的是，说清楚这门课不包含什么。"],[539.65,541.27,50,"We won't teach basic programming.","我们不教基础编程。"],[541.62,547.06,50,"We won't teach machine learning from scratch; if you need a refresher, please study on your own.","我们不从零教机器学习；如果需要补习，请自学。"],[547.41,555.43,50,"And we won't go deep into the mathematical theory of why NLP models work; this is a practical, systems-oriented course.","我们也不会深入讲 NLP 模型为何有效的数学理论；这是一门偏实践、偏系统的课。"],[555.78,561.82,50,"Some hot topics, like video generation models such as Sora, may not be covered either.","一些热门话题，比如 Sora 这样的视频生成模型，也可能不会讲。"],[562.17,566.53,50,"If you were hoping for those, there are other courses that do them well.","如果你期待这些内容，有其他课程讲得很好。"],[566.88,571.5,50,"Here, we focus on building and understanding language systems.","在这里，我们专注于构建和理解语言系统。"],[572.75,576.05,51,"How not to fail this course? It's actually simple.","怎样才不会挂掉这门课？其实很简单。"],[576.4,580.25,51,"Finish all assignments, the poster and the final report.","完成所有作业、海报和最终报告。"],[580.6,584.54,51,"Missing a component is the most common way to get a bad grade.","漏交某一部分，是拿低分最常见的原因。"],[584.89,588.1,51,"Be honest, even if your results are negative.","保持诚实，即使你的结果是负面的。"],[588.45,596.4,51,"A well-analyzed failure is much better than a fabricated success, and academic dishonesty is the one thing we won't tolerate.","一个分析透彻的失败远好过一个编造的成功，学术不端是我们绝不容忍的。"],[596.75,600.15,51,"And be nice to your teammates, classmates and TAs.","还有，善待你的队友、同学和助教。"],[600.5,605.32,51,"Most problems in team projects are people problems, not technical ones.","团队项目里的大多数问题是人的问题，而不是技术问题。"],[606.57,608.48,52,"And how do you really succeed?","那么怎样才能真正学好？"],[608.83,612.1,52,"Start your final project as early as possible.","尽早开始你的期末项目。"],[612.45,617.74,52,"Talk to the TAs and me frequently, for example after the lecture, from five pm.","经常和助教以及我交流，比如下课后，下午五点以后。"],[618.09,625.38,52,"Bring your own expertise, interests, users or data, and combine them with AI; that's your unfair advantage.","把你自己的专长、兴趣、用户或数据带进来，和 AI 结合，这就是你独特的优势。"],[625.73,628.34,52,"And aim higher than a grade.","目标要高于一个分数。"],[628.69,634.79,52,"A high-quality paper from this course could help you get a PhD offer or an internship.","这门课产出的一篇高质量论文，可能帮你拿到博士录取或实习机会。"],[635.14,640.13,52,"Or you might find future co-founders among your classmates and start a company.","或者你可能在同学中找到未来的联合创始人，一起创业。"],[640.48,643.61,52,"Treat the project as a launchpad, not just homework.","把项目当作发射台，而不只是作业。"],[644.86,650.73,53,"What can a great project bring you? Concretely, these are real outcomes from our group.","一个出色的项目能给你带来什么？具体来说，这些是我们组真实的成果。"],[651.08,658.56,53,"We can recommend strong students for internships at places like Qwen, Tencent, Huawei, DeepSeek and Kimi.","我们可以推荐优秀的学生去 Qwen、腾讯、华为、DeepSeek 和 Kimi 等地方实习。"],[658.91,666.44,53,"Our TAs have interned at companies such as Microsoft, Qwen, Tencent, Kimi, MiniMax and Huawei.","我们的助教曾在微软、Qwen、腾讯、Kimi、MiniMax 和华为等公司实习。"],[666.79,670.62,53,"We write recommendation letters for PhD applications.","我们会为申请博士的同学写推荐信。"],[670.97,675.2,53,"And some students have joined our group as PhD students.","还有一些同学加入了我们组读博。"],[675.55,685.7,53,"At the bottom you can see examples of students who did exactly that, along with the papers they published, including an ACL twenty twenty-five main conference paper.","最下面是几位这样的同学以及他们发表的论文，其中包括一篇 ACL 2025 主会论文。"],[686.05,691.51,53,"None of them started as experts. They started with a course project and kept going.","他们一开始都不是专家。他们从一个课程项目起步，然后坚持了下去。"]]},{"n":5,"title":"What Is NLP? Understanding, Generation and Core Tasks","blurb":"What natural language processing is, why natural language is special, NLU versus NLG, and the classic tasks: translation, dialogue, sentiment, classification, question answering and assistants.","file":"lecture01_part5.mp4","poster":"lecture01_part5.jpg","duration":626.1,"first":54,"last":67,"slides":[{"n":54,"title":"Contents","t":0.8},{"n":55,"title":"Natural Language Processing","t":23.96},{"n":56,"title":"What is NLP?","t":86.47},{"n":57,"title":"Why natural language instead of language","t":126.16},{"n":58,"title":"NLP — Natural Language “Processing” NLU — Natural Language “Understanding” NLG — Natural Language “Generation”","t":183.78},{"n":59,"title":"Go beyond the keyword matching","t":233.72},{"n":60,"title":"Machine translation","t":275.64},{"n":61,"title":"Dialog Systems","t":321.23},{"n":62,"title":"Sentiment/Opinion Analysis","t":358.07},{"n":63,"title":"Text Classification","t":403.23},{"n":64,"title":"Question answering","t":449.71},{"n":65,"title":"Question answering","t":501.75},{"n":66,"title":"Natural language instruction Digital personal assistant","t":539.68},{"n":67,"title":"The NLP would be much broader!","t":584.45}],"sents":[[0.8,5.48,54,"That's the end of the logistics part. Thank you for your patience; now for the fun part.","课程安排部分到此结束。谢谢大家的耐心，接下来是有趣的部分。"],[5.83,8.58,54,"In this third section, we answer two questions.","在第三部分，我们回答两个问题。"],[8.93,13.82,54,"First, what is natural language processing, and what kinds of problems does it solve?","第一，什么是自然语言处理，它解决哪些问题？"],[14.17,22.56,54,"Second, how did the field evolve from hand-built rules and pipelines to the large language models and agents we use today?","第二，这个领域是如何从手工规则和流水线，演进到今天我们使用的大语言模型和智能体的？"],[23.81,28.5,55,"Let's start with the big picture of the field. NLP has two sides.","我们先看这个领域的全景。NLP 有两个方面。"],[28.85,33.33,55,"On the left are applications, the things users actually see.","左边是应用，也就是用户真正看得到的东西。"],[33.68,43.47,55,"Machine translation, search, question answering, dialogue systems, information extraction, summarization, sentiment analysis, and many more.","机器翻译、搜索、问答、对话系统、信息抽取、摘要、情感分析等等。"],[43.82,48.14,55,"On the right are core technologies, the building blocks underneath.","右边是核心技术，也就是底层的构建模块。"],[48.49,57.64,55,"Language modeling, part-of-speech tagging, parsing, named-entity recognition, word sense disambiguation, and semantic role labeling.","语言建模、词性标注、句法分析、命名实体识别、词义消歧，以及语义角色标注。"],[57.99,63.53,55,"For decades, building an application meant chaining many of these core components together.","几十年来，做一个应用就意味着把许多这样的核心组件串联起来。"],[63.88,70.4,55,"And remember the red line: NLP sits at the intersection of computational linguistics and machine learning.","记住这行红字：NLP 位于计算语言学和机器学习的交叉点。"],[70.75,76.27,55,"Linguistics tells us what structure language has; machine learning lets us learn it from data.","语言学告诉我们语言有什么结构，机器学习让我们从数据中学到它。"],[76.62,85.07,55,"Keep the language modeling item in mind, because by the end of today it will have swallowed almost everything else on this slide.","记住“语言建模”这一项，因为到今天课程结束时，它几乎会吞掉这张幻灯片上的其他所有内容。"],[86.32,88.62,56,"So what is NLP, formally?","那么，正式地说，什么是 NLP？"],[88.97,98.88,56,"The classic definition: a field of computer science, AI and computational linguistics, concerned with the interactions between computers and human, or natural, language.","经典定义是：计算机科学、人工智能和计算语言学的一个领域，研究计算机与人类语言，也就是自然语言之间的交互。"],[99.23,100.44,56,"I love this picture.","我很喜欢这张图。"],[100.79,108.33,56,"C-3PO, the protocol droid from Star Wars, is teaching a language lesson, translating Huttese words into English.","《星球大战》里的礼仪机器人 C-3PO 正在上语言课，把赫特语单词翻译成英语。"],[108.68,116.79,56,"In a way, that's the dream of NLP: a machine fluent in human languages that can translate, explain and converse.","某种意义上，这就是 NLP 的梦想：一台精通人类语言、能翻译、能解释、能对话的机器。"],[117.14,119.76,56,"Notice the word natural in bold.","注意加粗的“natural”这个词。"],[120.11,124.76,56,"Why do we say natural language, and not just language? That's next.","为什么要说“自然语言”，而不只是“语言”？我们接着看。"],[126.01,131.63,57,"The word natural is there to contrast with formal languages, like programming languages.","“自然”这个词，是为了和形式语言，比如编程语言，相区分。"],[131.98,139.39,57,"A programming language is designed: its grammar is precise, and every statement has exactly one meaning.","编程语言是设计出来的：语法精确，每条语句只有唯一的含义。"],[139.74,147.66,57,"Natural language evolved: it's ambiguous, context-dependent, and full of idioms, sarcasm and exceptions.","自然语言是演化而来的：它有歧义、依赖上下文，充满习语、讽刺和例外。"],[148.01,151.86,57,"Take the sentence: I saw the man with the telescope.","比如这句话：I saw the man with the telescope。"],[152.21,158.56,57,"Who has the telescope, me or the man? It has two meanings, and a compiler would just give up.","望远镜在谁手里，是我还是那个人？它有两种含义，编译器只能放弃。"],[158.91,163.18,57,"That ambiguity is what makes NLP hard and interesting.","正是这种歧义，让 NLP 既困难又有趣。"],[163.53,168.18,57,"But here's a twist: in the LLM era, the boundary is blurring.","但有个转折：在大模型时代，这条边界正在变得模糊。"],[168.53,174.89,57,"The same models that read English also read and write Python, so NLP today also covers code.","能读英语的模型同样能读写 Python，所以今天的 NLP 也涵盖代码。"],[175.24,182.38,57,"My colleague Professor Pinjia He works on exactly this intersection of language models and software, if you're interested.","我的同事何品佳教授正是研究语言模型与软件这一交叉方向的，感兴趣的同学可以了解一下。"],[183.63,189.89,58,"A useful way to split NLP is this equation: NLP equals NLU plus NLG.","一个划分 NLP 的好办法是这个等式：NLP 等于 NLU 加 NLG。"],[190.24,193.64,58,"Natural language understanding goes from text to meaning.","自然语言理解，是从文本到含义。"],[193.99,201.59,58,"That means reading a sentence and figuring out what it says: who did what to whom, and what the intent is.","也就是读一个句子，弄清它在说什么：谁对谁做了什么，意图是什么。"],[201.94,208.79,58,"Natural language generation goes the other way, from meaning to text, producing fluent language that expresses something.","自然语言生成则反过来，从含义到文本，产出流畅的语言来表达某种意思。"],[209.14,214.78,58,"Look at the diagram: text goes up into some internal meaning, and comes back down as text.","看这张图：文本向上进入某种内部含义，再向下变回文本。"],[215.13,219.15,58,"Translation, summarization and dialogue all fit this shape.","翻译、摘要和对话都符合这个形状。"],[219.5,224.5,58,"Historically, these were separate research communities with separate models.","历史上，这两者是各自独立的研究社区，用的也是各自的模型。"],[224.85,232.32,58,"One remarkable thing about modern LLMs is that a single model does both, and we'll see why when we get to language modeling.","现代大模型的一个了不起之处在于，一个模型就能同时做到两者，讲到语言建模时我们会看到原因。"],[233.57,235.97,59,"Here's why understanding language is hard.","这就是为什么理解语言很难。"],[236.32,240.69,59,"This cartoon shows what we say to dogs, versus what they hear.","这幅漫画展示了我们对狗说的话，和狗实际听到的话。"],[241.04,246.68,59,"We say a whole sentence about staying out of the garbage, and the dog hears: blah blah Ginger, blah blah.","我们说了一整句让它别去翻垃圾的话，而狗听到的是：叽里咕噜 Ginger，叽里咕噜。"],[247.03,250.44,59,"That's exactly how early keyword-based systems worked.","早期基于关键词的系统正是这样工作的。"],[250.79,256.15,59,"A search engine matching keywords is the dog: it catches Ginger, and misses everything else.","做关键词匹配的搜索引擎就像这只狗：它只抓住了 Ginger，其他的全都错过了。"],[256.5,259.78,59,"Real NLP has to go beyond keyword matching.","真正的自然语言处理必须超越关键词匹配。"],[260.13,266.81,59,"It has to identify the structure and meaning of words, sentences, whole documents and conversations.","它必须识别词语、句子、整篇文档乃至对话的结构和含义。"],[267.16,271.9,59,"And when it works, it's everywhere around us, often invisibly.","而当它真正奏效时，它就无处不在，而且常常是无形的。"],[272.25,274.24,59,"Let me show you some examples.","我来给大家看几个例子。"],[275.49,282.18,60,"Machine translation is the classic NLP application, and one of the oldest dreams of AI.","机器翻译是最经典的 NLP 应用，也是人工智能最古老的梦想之一。"],[282.53,288.55,60,"On the bottom left, a simple case: buenas noches becomes Goodnight. Easy.","左下角是一个简单的例子：buenas noches 被翻译成 Goodnight。很简单。"],[288.9,294.48,60,"But look at the right side: a Facebook post in Hebrew, automatically translated into English.","但看右边：一条希伯来语的 Facebook 帖子，被自动翻译成了英语。"],[294.83,299.68,60,"The result is barely readable, with broken phrases and untranslated words.","结果几乎没法读，短语支离破碎，还有没翻译出来的词。"],[300.03,306.22,60,"This is what machine translation looked like not so long ago, for harder language pairs and informal text.","不久之前，对于较难的语言对和非正式文本，机器翻译就是这个样子。"],[306.57,307.85,60,"Keep this picture in mind.","请记住这幅画面。"],[308.2,312.86,60,"Today's LLMs translate that kind of text far more fluently.","今天的大语言模型翻译这类文本要流畅得多。"],[313.21,319.83,60,"And the gap between these two screenshots and what you can do now is a good measure of how far the field has come.","这两张截图和你现在能做到的之间的差距，很好地衡量了这个领域走了多远。"],[321.08,324.44,61,"Dialog systems are another core application.","对话系统是另一个核心应用。"],[324.79,334.17,61,"This screenshot shows an old-style automated online assistant on a website: a friendly face, and a text box asking how it may help you.","这张截图展示的是网站上一个老式的自动在线助手：一张友好的面孔，加一个询问能帮你什么的文本框。"],[334.52,338.77,61,"Systems like this were mostly built from rules and scripted flows.","这类系统大多由规则和预设的脚本流程构建而成。"],[339.12,344.0,61,"They worked for a handful of anticipated questions, and failed badly on anything else.","它们只能应付少数预料之中的问题，碰到其他问题就一败涂地。"],[344.35,349.33,61,"If you've ever shouted talk to a human at a customer-service bot, you know the feeling.","如果你曾经对着客服机器人大喊“转人工”，你就懂这种感觉。"],[349.68,356.67,61,"Compare that to chatting with a modern LLM assistant, and you'll see why dialogue has become the main interface to AI.","把它和现在的大模型助手聊天对比一下，你就会明白为什么对话已经成为使用 AI 的主要界面。"],[357.92,364.17,62,"Sentiment or opinion analysis means figuring out how people feel from what they write.","情感分析或观点分析，就是从人们写的文字中判断他们的感受。"],[364.52,366.73,62,"This tool tracked opinions on Twitter.","这个工具用来追踪 Twitter 上的观点。"],[367.08,371.87,62,"Searching for Starbucks, it split the tweets into positive, neutral and negative.","搜索 Starbucks 时，它把推文分成了正面、中性和负面三类。"],[372.22,379.75,62,"Look at the numbers: about eighty-three percent are neutral, thirteen percent positive, and only about four percent negative.","看这些数字：大约 83% 是中性的，13% 是正面的，只有大约 4% 是负面的。"],[380.1,385.63,62,"Companies use this for brand monitoring, product feedback, and even financial signals.","企业用它来做品牌监测、收集产品反馈，甚至获取金融信号。"],[385.98,388.04,62,"It's harder than it looks.","这件事比看起来要难。"],[388.39,398.01,62,"Look at the example tweets: sarcasm, mixed feelings, or a negative word that isn't actually about the brand can all fool a simple classifier.","看看这些推文例子：讽刺、复杂的情绪，或者一个其实与品牌无关的负面词，都可能骗过简单的分类器。"],[398.36,401.83,62,"Language carries emotion in very subtle ways.","语言承载情感的方式非常微妙。"],[403.08,409.2,63,"Text classification is probably the most widely deployed NLP task, and you use it every day.","文本分类可能是部署最广泛的 NLP 任务，你每天都在用它。"],[409.55,412.11,63,"Spam filtering is the classic example.","垃圾邮件过滤就是经典例子。"],[412.46,420.55,63,"Gmail sorting your inbox into Primary, Social, Promotions and Updates is classification too.","Gmail 把你的收件箱分成主要、社交、推广和动态，这也是分类。"],[420.9,429.54,63,"And the pop-up at the top is a nice one: you wrote is attached, but didn't attach anything, so Gmail asks whether you forgot.","上面这个弹窗很有意思：你写了“见附件”，却没有添加任何附件，于是 Gmail 问你是不是忘了。"],[429.89,434.08,63,"That's a tiny piece of language understanding, preventing an embarrassing email.","这是一小段语言理解，帮你避免了一封尴尬的邮件。"],[434.43,437.13,63,"The slide asks: other applications?","幻灯片上问：还有其他应用吗？"],[437.48,439.52,63,"Take a moment and think of a few.","花点时间想几个。"],[439.87,448.31,63,"News categorization, routing support tickets, detecting toxic comments, triaging medical messages; there are countless more.","新闻分类、客服工单分派、有害评论检测、医疗消息分诊；还有数不清的应用。"],[449.56,451.57,64,"Next, question answering.","接下来是问答。"],[451.92,458.66,64,"In two thousand eleven, IBM's Watson beat two of the greatest human champions on the quiz show Jeopardy.","2011 年，IBM 的 Watson 在智力竞赛节目 Jeopardy 中击败了两位最强的人类冠军。"],[459.01,461.15,64,"That was a landmark moment for NLP.","那是 NLP 的一个里程碑时刻。"],[461.5,465.6,64,"But look at the questions on the right; they get progressively harder.","但看看右边这些问题，它们一个比一个难。"],[465.95,468.87,64,"What does divergent mean? That's a dictionary lookup.","“divergent”是什么意思？这只需要查字典。"],[469.22,472.4,64,"What year was Lincoln born? A simple fact.","林肯是哪一年出生的？一个简单的事实。"],[472.75,477.45,64,"How many US states were there that year? Now you need to chain two facts.","那一年美国有多少个州？现在你需要把两个事实串起来。"],[477.8,486.36,64,"How much Chinese silk was exported to England at the end of the eighteenth century? You need to find and aggregate obscure historical data.","十八世纪末有多少中国丝绸出口到英国？你需要查找并汇总冷僻的历史数据。"],[486.71,493.93,64,"What do scientists think about the ethics of human cloning? There's no single answer at all; you have to summarize opinions.","科学家如何看待人类克隆的伦理？这根本没有唯一答案，你得去归纳各方观点。"],[494.28,500.35,64,"That ladder, from lookup to reasoning to synthesis, is a nice map of how hard QA can get.","这个阶梯，从查找到推理再到综合，很好地描绘了问答可以有多难。"],[501.6,506.5,65,"Question answering is also how search engines went beyond search.","问答也是搜索引擎超越“搜索”本身的方式。"],[506.85,509.26,65,"Ask: what's the capital of Wyoming?","问一句：怀俄明州的首府是哪里？"],[509.61,515.12,65,"Instead of just ten blue links, you get a direct answer, Cheyenne, with a photo and a map.","你得到的不只是十条蓝色链接，而是一个直接的答案：夏延，还配有照片和地图。"],[515.47,525.19,65,"The system had to understand the question, recognize Wyoming as an entity and capital as a relation, and look up the answer in a knowledge base.","系统必须理解问题，识别出怀俄明是一个实体、首府是一种关系，再到知识库里查出答案。"],[525.54,531.48,65,"This was a big shift: from finding documents that might contain the answer, to giving you the answer.","这是一个巨大的转变：从找出可能包含答案的文档，到直接给你答案。"],[531.83,538.28,65,"LLM-powered search engines today push this even further, writing a full response with citations.","今天由大模型驱动的搜索引擎更进一步，能写出带引用的完整回答。"],[539.53,545.06,66,"Then came digital personal assistants that follow natural language instructions.","随后出现了能听懂自然语言指令的数字个人助手。"],[545.41,549.05,66,"On the left is a smart speaker surrounded by typical requests.","左边是一个智能音箱，周围是一些典型的请求。"],[549.4,555.28,66,"Will it rain tomorrow? Set an alarm. Play some music. Add gelato to my shopping list.","明天会下雨吗？定个闹钟。放点音乐。把意式冰淇淋加到购物清单里。"],[555.63,559.58,66,"On the right is a phone assistant asking: what can I help you do now?","右边是一个手机助手在问：现在我能帮你做什么？"],[559.93,563.53,66,"For the first time, millions of people talked to a machine every day.","这是第一次，数以百万计的人每天都在和机器说话。"],[563.88,569.07,66,"Notice that these requests are mostly short commands mapped to fixed actions.","注意，这些请求大多是短指令，对应到固定的操作上。"],[569.42,574.93,66,"These assistants were useful but brittle; step outside the expected phrasing and they'd fail.","这些助手有用但很脆弱；说法稍微超出预期，它们就会失败。"],[575.28,583.05,66,"Today's LLM-based assistants can handle open-ended, multi-step requests, which is a big leap.","今天基于大模型的助手能处理开放式、多步骤的请求，这是一个巨大的飞跃。"],[584.3,592.56,67,"So far I've shown you classic applications: translation, dialogue, sentiment, classification, question answering and assistants.","到目前为止，我给大家展示的是经典应用：翻译、对话、情感分析、分类、问答和助手。"],[592.91,597.95,67,"But here's the key message: NLP today is much broader than this list.","但关键信息是：今天的 NLP 远比这份清单广泛。"],[598.3,603.58,67,"Once a model truly works with language, language becomes a universal interface.","一旦模型真正掌握了语言，语言就成了一种通用接口。"],[603.93,611.68,67,"You can describe almost any task in words: write code, analyze a medical record, plan a trip, control a robot.","几乎任何任务都可以用文字描述：写代码、分析病历、规划旅行、控制机器人。"],[612.03,619.3,67,"So NLP is no longer one subfield of AI among many; in many ways, it has become the front door to AI.","所以 NLP 不再只是 AI 众多子领域之一；在很多方面，它已经成为通往 AI 的大门。"],[619.65,624.21,67,"To understand how we got here, let's look at how the field evolved.","要理解我们是怎么走到这一步的，我们来看看这个领域是如何演进的。"]]},{"n":6,"title":"From Pipelines to Transformers: A Brief History of NLP","blurb":"How NLP evolved from rules and task-specific pipelines through the Transformer era to today's assistants, and the question of how old NLP turned into large language models.","file":"lecture01_part6.mp4","poster":"lecture01_part6.jpg","duration":347.7,"first":68,"last":75,"slides":[{"n":68,"title":"Pre-transformer era of NLP","t":0.8},{"n":69,"title":"A brief timeline of the evolution of NLP","t":55.05},{"n":70,"title":"Transformer era of NLP","t":112.45},{"n":71,"title":"Where Are We Now?","t":158.4},{"n":72,"title":"https://www.douyin.com/video/7461889667558886690","t":201.4},{"n":73,"title":"Personal assistant: Her","t":239.14},{"n":74,"title":"Her with video generation","t":278.27},{"n":75,"title":"From old NLP to Large Language models (LLMs)?","t":321.89}],"sents":[[0.8,5.49,68,"Let's go back to the pre-Transformer era of NLP. How did we build systems then?","我们回到 Transformer 之前的 NLP 时代。那时候我们是怎么构建系统的？"],[5.84,12.75,68,"Look at the left: to understand find me an Italian restaurant in New York City, a system would tag each piece.","看左边：为了理解“帮我找一家纽约市的意大利餐厅”，系统会给每个片段打标签。"],[13.1,18.35,68,"Find is the action, Italian is the food type, and New York City is the location.","“找”是动作，“意大利”是菜系，“纽约市”是地点。"],[18.7,25.74,68,"Then for the follow-up, what's the weather there tomorrow, it must figure out that there refers back to New York.","接着对于追问“明天那里天气怎么样”，它必须弄清楚“那里”指的是纽约。"],[26.09,32.63,68,"Below is a syntactic parse tree, breaking a sentence into noun phrases, verb phrases and so on.","下面是一棵句法分析树，把句子拆成名词短语、动词短语等等。"],[32.98,41.79,68,"On the right is the typical pipeline: segmentation, part-of-speech tagging, entity extraction, word sense disambiguation, and parsing.","右边是典型的流水线：分词、词性标注、实体抽取、词义消歧和句法分析。"],[42.14,48.22,68,"Then coreference, relation and event extraction, all stacked, and finally stored in a database.","然后是指代消解、关系抽取和事件抽取，层层堆叠，最后存进数据库。"],[48.57,53.65,68,"Every stage was a separate model, and errors added up as you went down the stack.","每个阶段都是一个独立的模型，越往下走，错误累积得越多。"],[54.9,58.91,69,"Here's a brief timeline of NLP, with the main milestones.","这是一条简要的 NLP 时间线，标出了主要的里程碑。"],[59.26,65.19,69,"On the far left, the bag-of-words idea: represent text simply by counting words, ignoring order.","最左边是词袋模型的思想：只靠统计词频来表示文本，忽略词序。"],[65.54,70.97,69,"Then TF-IDF, which weights words by how informative they are.","然后是 TF-IDF，它按照词语的信息量给词加权。"],[71.32,75.83,69,"RNNs and LSTMs brought sequence modeling with memory.","RNN 和 LSTM 带来了有记忆的序列建模。"],[76.18,83.76,69,"In two thousand three, the neural probabilistic language model first used neural networks and word embeddings for language modeling.","2003 年，神经概率语言模型首次把神经网络和词向量用于语言建模。"],[84.11,89.53,69,"Word2vec in two thousand thirteen made word embeddings cheap and popular.","2013 年的 Word2vec 让词向量变得廉价而流行。"],[89.88,97.57,69,"Then in two thousand seventeen came the Transformer, followed by BERT, GPT-3, ChatGPT and GPT-4.","接着 2017 年出现了 Transformer，随后是 BERT、GPT-3、ChatGPT 和 GPT-4。"],[97.92,100.61,69,"The thing to notice is the accelerating pace.","值得注意的是不断加快的节奏。"],[100.96,107.28,69,"Decades separate the early milestones; at the right end, major breakthroughs come every year or two.","早期的里程碑之间相隔几十年；而在右端，每一两年就有一次重大突破。"],[107.63,111.05,69,"Each of these will appear again in our upcoming lectures.","这里的每一个都会在后续课程中再次出现。"],[112.3,116.85,70,"You can think of this history as an evolution, like this famous picture.","你可以把这段历史看作一场进化，就像这幅著名的图一样。"],[117.2,122.78,70,"First came rule-based systems, where experts hand-wrote grammar rules and dictionaries.","最先出现的是基于规则的系统，由专家手工编写语法规则和词典。"],[123.13,127.3,70,"Then statistical models, learning probabilities from data.","然后是统计模型，从数据中学习概率。"],[127.65,133.07,70,"Then deep learning models, learning representations automatically with neural networks.","再然后是深度学习模型，用神经网络自动学习表示。"],[133.42,140.02,70,"And finally Transformer models, the architecture on the right, which is the basis of every modern LLM.","最后是 Transformer 模型，也就是右边这个架构，它是所有现代大模型的基础。"],[140.37,146.71,70,"Each step reduced how much humans had to specify by hand, and increased how much the model learned from data.","每一步都减少了人类需要手工指定的东西，增加了模型从数据中学到的东西。"],[147.06,151.26,70,"We'll open up that Transformer diagram piece by piece in Lecture four.","我们会在第四讲把这张 Transformer 结构图一块一块地拆开讲。"],[151.61,157.0,70,"For now, just remember that this one architecture is what made the current era possible.","现在只需要记住：正是这一个架构，成就了当今这个时代。"],[158.25,159.74,71,"So where are we now?","那么，我们现在走到哪一步了？"],[160.09,167.94,71,"On the left are today's assistants: ChatGPT, with GPT-5 behind it, and a Chinese assistant app with a friendly avatar.","左边是今天的助手：背后是 GPT-5 的 ChatGPT，以及一款有着亲切头像的中国助手应用。"],[168.29,172.78,71,"On the right is the poster of the movie Her, from two thousand thirteen.","右边是 2013 年电影《Her》的海报。"],[173.13,182.62,71,"In it, a man falls in love with an AI operating system called Samantha, who talks to him naturally, understands his emotions and organizes his life.","片中，一个男人爱上了名叫 Samantha 的 AI 操作系统，她能自然地和他交谈、理解他的情绪、打理他的生活。"],[182.97,186.71,71,"When that movie came out, it felt like pure science fiction.","这部电影上映时，看起来完全是科幻。"],[187.06,193.41,71,"Today, many people chat with AI by voice every day, for work, study and even emotional support.","而今天，很多人每天都在用语音和 AI 聊天，为了工作、学习，甚至情感支持。"],[193.76,198.19,71,"The question I'd like you to think about is: how close are we to Samantha?","我希望大家思考的问题是：我们离 Samantha 还有多远？"],[198.54,200.0,71,"And what's still missing?","还缺些什么？"],[201.25,205.96,72,"Here is a scene from a short video that makes that question concrete.","这是一段短视频里的画面，它让这个问题变得具体。"],[206.31,212.66,72,"Notice the everyday setting: a home decorated for the festival, and an ordinary person going about her day.","注意这个日常场景：一个布置得很有节日气氛的家，一位普通人在过着她的日子。"],[213.01,216.08,72,"AI isn't something only engineers use anymore.","AI 不再只是工程师才用的东西。"],[216.43,222.44,72,"It's showing up in family life, in companionship, and in how people get through daily routines.","它正出现在家庭生活里、陪伴中，以及人们度过日常的方式里。"],[222.79,232.8,72,"So think about this: what would an AI need to understand, about language, about emotion, about context, to really be helpful in a scene like this?","那么请想一想：在这样的场景中，AI 需要理解哪些语言、情感和语境，才能真正帮上忙？"],[233.15,237.74,72,"That's exactly the gap between today's chatbots and the vision in Her.","这正是今天的聊天机器人与《Her》中的愿景之间的差距。"],[238.99,243.56,73,"Here's a clip from Her itself, showing Samantha as a personal assistant.","这是《Her》本身的一个片段，展示了 Samantha 作为私人助理的样子。"],[243.91,245.9,73,"Pay attention to what she does.","注意她做了些什么。"],[246.25,256.56,73,"She understands vague, emotional, spoken language, remembers context, has a personality, and takes actions in the user's life, like sorting emails.","她能理解模糊的、带情绪的口语，记得上下文，有自己的个性，还能在用户的生活中采取行动，比如整理邮件。"],[256.91,262.77,73,"That's natural language understanding, generation, memory and agency, all in one.","这就是把自然语言理解、生成、记忆和行动能力集于一身。"],[263.12,266.22,73,"If you haven't seen the movie, I really recommend it.","如果你还没看过这部电影，我真心推荐。"],[266.57,270.35,73,"It's one of the best thought experiments about where NLP is heading.","它是关于 NLP 未来走向的最好的思想实验之一。"],[270.7,276.87,73,"And many of its scenes now look less like fiction and more like product roadmaps.","而它的很多场景，现在看起来不太像科幻，倒更像产品路线图。"],[278.12,280.97,74,"And it's not just voice anymore.","而且现在已经不只是声音了。"],[281.32,289.14,74,"This project is literally called Body of Her: giving the AI companion a visible body through video generation.","这个项目就叫 Body of Her：通过视频生成，给 AI 伴侣一个看得见的身体。"],[289.49,298.88,74,"On the left is the human user; on the right is the agent, a generated video character that reacts and moves in real time as the conversation goes on.","左边是人类用户；右边是智能体，一个生成出来的视频角色，会随着对话实时做出反应和动作。"],[299.23,305.78,74,"So the AI doesn't only talk; it can show facial expressions and gestures.","所以 AI 不只会说话，还能展现面部表情和手势。"],[306.13,309.63,74,"This is where NLP meets vision and video generation.","这就是 NLP 与视觉和视频生成交汇的地方。"],[309.98,312.96,74,"We'll come back to multimodal models later in the semester.","我们会在这学期后面再回到多模态模型。"],[313.31,320.49,74,"The broader point: language is the backbone, but the interface is becoming richer and more human-like.","更大的要点是：语言是骨架，但交互界面正变得越来越丰富、越来越像人。"],[321.74,325.27,75,"We've seen what NLP does and how far it has come.","我们已经看到了 NLP 能做什么，以及它走了多远。"],[325.62,331.8,75,"Now let's ask the central question of this section: how did we get from old NLP to large language models?","现在我们来问这一部分的核心问题：我们是如何从传统 NLP 走到大语言模型的？"],[332.15,337.3,75,"The short answer is one idea, language modeling, scaled up enormously.","简短的回答是一个想法：语言建模，再把它极大地扩展规模。"],[337.65,345.81,75,"In the next few slides, I'll explain what a language model is, why that simple objective is so powerful, and what large really means.","接下来几页，我会解释什么是语言模型、为什么这个简单的目标如此强大，以及“大”到底意味着什么。"]]},{"n":7,"title":"Language Models, LLMs and the Step to Agents","blurb":"What language modeling is, from n-grams to neural networks, narrow and broad senses of language models, PLMs versus LLMs, what makes them large, and how LLMs become agents.","file":"lecture01_part7.mp4","poster":"lecture01_part7.jpg","duration":858.5,"first":76,"last":92,"slides":[{"n":76,"title":"Background","t":0.8},{"n":77,"title":"What is language modeling?","t":69.93},{"n":78,"title":"What is language modeling?","t":104.04},{"n":79,"title":"What is language modeling?","t":150.85},{"n":80,"title":"What is language modeling?","t":198.08},{"n":81,"title":"Language model using neural networks","t":247.82},{"n":82,"title":"Language models: Narrow Sense","t":299.25},{"n":83,"title":"Language models:Broad Sense","t":353.17},{"n":84,"title":"PLM vs. LLM","t":412.93},{"n":85,"title":"Some basics for large language models","t":473.75},{"n":86,"title":"Large Language Models","t":532.92},{"n":87,"title":"Large Language Models - Hundreds of Billions of Tokens","t":591.0},{"n":88,"title":"How Large are “Large” LMs?","t":641.38},{"n":89,"title":"From LLMs to Agent","t":702.21},{"n":90,"title":"Mobile Agent","t":727.31},{"n":91,"title":"Game Agent","t":771.03},{"n":92,"title":"Embodied AI","t":814.6}],"sents":[[0.8,7.02,76,"First, some background. Here's a timeline focused on language models and word representations.","首先是一些背景。这是一条聚焦于语言模型和词表示的时间线。"],[7.37,15.09,76,"In nineteen forty-eight, the n-gram model, going back to Shannon: predict the next item from the previous n minus one.","1948 年，n 元语法模型，可以追溯到香农：根据前 n 减 1 个元素预测下一个。"],[15.44,22.34,76,"In nineteen fifty-four, the distributional hypothesis: a word is characterized by the company it keeps.","1954 年，分布式假说：一个词的含义由它周围的词来刻画。"],[22.69,28.94,76,"That one sentence is the philosophical basis of everything from word2vec to GPT.","这一句话，就是从 word2vec 到 GPT 一切的哲学基础。"],[29.29,32.02,76,"Bag-of-words comes from the same period.","词袋模型也来自同一时期。"],[32.37,41.74,76,"In nineteen eighty-six, distributed representations: represent a concept as a pattern across many units, rather than one symbol.","1986 年，分布式表示：把一个概念表示为许多单元上的激活模式，而不是单个符号。"],[42.09,46.88,76,"In two thousand three, the neural probabilistic language model put these together.","2003 年，神经概率语言模型把这些结合到了一起。"],[47.23,51.4,76,"In two thousand thirteen, word2vec made embeddings efficient.","2013 年，word2vec 让词向量变得高效。"],[51.75,60.21,76,"And in two thousand eighteen, pre-trained language models brought contextual representations and the pre-train-then-fine-tune paradigm.","而在 2018 年，预训练语言模型带来了上下文相关的表示，以及“先预训练、再微调”的范式。"],[60.56,68.53,76,"So LLMs aren't a sudden invention. They're the result of seventy years of accumulating ideas.","所以大模型并不是突然的发明，而是七十年思想积累的结果。"],[69.78,71.98,77,"So, what is language modeling?","那么，什么是语言建模？"],[72.33,77.17,77,"The basic definition: a language model assigns a probability to a sequence of words.","基本定义是：语言模型为一个词序列赋予一个概率。"],[77.52,83.88,77,"Formally, f maps a sequence of n words from the vocabulary V to a positive real number.","形式化地说，f 把来自词表 V 的 n 个词组成的序列映射到一个正实数。"],[84.23,90.04,77,"V to the power n just means any sequence of n words, and the output is how likely that sequence is.","V 的 n 次方就是指任意 n 个词的序列，输出则是这个序列出现的可能性。"],[90.39,95.0,77,"That sounds very abstract, almost boring. A function that scores sentences?","这听起来非常抽象，甚至有点无聊。一个给句子打分的函数？"],[95.35,100.51,77,"But hold on, because this simple definition turns out to be the foundation of ChatGPT.","但先别急，因为这个简单的定义恰恰是 ChatGPT 的基础。"],[100.86,102.64,77,"Let me make it concrete.","我来把它讲具体一点。"],[103.89,105.16,78,"Here's the intuition.","直觉是这样的。"],[105.51,109.31,78,"Imagine a chimpanzee randomly hitting typewriter keys.","想象一只黑猩猩在打字机上乱敲键盘。"],[109.66,113.58,78,"It produces something like this string of random letters.","它打出来的就是这样一串随机字母。"],[113.93,120.5,78,"A good language model should assign that a very low probability; it doesn't look like human language at all.","一个好的语言模型应该给它一个很低的概率；它看起来完全不像人类语言。"],[120.85,124.6,78,"Now a person types: ChatGPT is all you need.","现在一个人打出：ChatGPT is all you need。"],[124.95,129.75,78,"That's a fluent, plausible English sentence, so it gets a high probability.","这是一个通顺、合理的英语句子，所以它得到一个高概率。"],[130.1,134.8,78,"So a language model is essentially a model of what real language looks like.","所以，语言模型本质上是对真实语言长什么样的建模。"],[135.15,143.59,78,"To assign these probabilities well, it has to implicitly know spelling, grammar, common phrases, even facts about the world.","要把这些概率给好，它必须隐式地掌握拼写、语法、常用短语，甚至关于世界的知识。"],[143.94,149.45,78,"That's why something as simple as scoring sentences ends up capturing so much knowledge.","这就是为什么像给句子打分这样简单的事，最终能捕获如此多的知识。"],[150.7,159.9,79,"The more useful form is the conditional language model: instead of scoring a whole sentence, predict the next word given the words before it.","更有用的形式是条件语言模型：不是给整句打分，而是根据前面的词预测下一个词。"],[160.25,166.05,79,"That's g, which takes the previous n minus one words and a candidate word, and returns a score.","这就是 g：它接收前 n 减 1 个词和一个候选词，返回一个分数。"],[166.4,167.88,79,"You use this every day.","你每天都在用它。"],[168.23,174.44,79,"Look at the input method example: you type I've, and the keyboard suggests been, got, never.","看这个输入法的例子：你输入 I've，键盘就推荐 been、got、never。"],[174.79,179.28,79,"That's a conditional language model choosing the most likely next words.","这就是一个条件语言模型在挑选最可能的下一个词。"],[179.63,182.09,79,"And here is the connection between the two.","这两者之间的联系是这样的。"],[182.44,190.73,79,"The probability of the next word given the history equals the probability of the full sequence, divided by the probability of the history.","给定历史时下一个词的概率，等于整个序列的概率除以历史部分的概率。"],[191.08,196.68,79,"In plain words: how likely is the whole thing, relative to how likely the beginning was.","通俗地说就是：整句话的可能性，相对于开头部分的可能性有多大。"],[197.93,204.28,80,"Here's the complete formula: p of w n, given w one through w n minus one.","这是完整的公式：给定 w1 到 w n 减 1 时，w n 的概率。"],[204.63,209.35,80,"Read it as: the probability of the next word, given everything that came before.","可以读作：给定前面所有内容时，下一个词的概率。"],[209.7,214.52,80,"And this line at the bottom is the single most important sentence in today's lecture.","而底部这一行，是今天这堂课中最重要的一句话。"],[214.87,221.71,80,"This conditional probability is the foundation of modern large language models: GPT, ChatGPT and so on.","这个条件概率是现代大语言模型的基础：GPT、ChatGPT 等等。"],[222.06,227.09,80,"When ChatGPT writes you an essay, it's doing exactly this, over and over.","当 ChatGPT 为你写一篇文章时，它做的正是这件事，一遍又一遍。"],[227.44,234.92,80,"It computes a probability distribution over the next token given everything so far, picks one, appends it, and repeats.","它根据已有的全部内容计算下一个 token 的概率分布，选出一个，接到后面，然后重复。"],[235.27,242.53,80,"Everything else, the reasoning, the conversation, the code, emerges from doing this one thing extremely well.","其他一切，推理、对话、代码，都是从把这一件事做到极致中涌现出来的。"],[242.88,246.42,80,"We'll spend all of Lecture three on it.","我们会用整个第三讲来讲它。"],[247.67,251.81,81,"How do we actually compute that probability? Today, with neural networks.","那么这个概率到底怎么算？今天，我们用神经网络。"],[252.16,253.57,81,"Here's the picture.","看这张图。"],[253.92,261.68,81,"The input is a Chinese sentence, wo si gu wo zai, I think, therefore I am, with the last character missing.","输入是一句中文“我思故我在”，也就是 I think, therefore I am，但缺了最后一个字。"],[262.03,266.87,81,"The words go in at the bottom and pass through layers of a neural network.","这些字从底部输入，经过神经网络的一层又一层。"],[267.22,271.32,81,"At the top, the network predicts the next character: zai.","在顶部，网络预测出下一个字：“在”。"],[271.67,277.89,81,"Inside, it's a black box: millions or billions of numbers transforming the input step by step.","内部是一个黑箱：数百万乃至数十亿个数字，一步步地变换输入。"],[278.24,287.94,81,"The callout gives you a sense of scale: GPT-3 has one hundred seventy-five billion parameters, and the human brain has on the order of a hundred billion neurons.","旁边的标注让你感受一下规模：GPT-3 有 1750 亿个参数，而人脑大约有上千亿个神经元。"],[288.29,292.29,81,"The comparison is loose, since a parameter is not a neuron.","这个比较并不严格，因为一个参数不等于一个神经元。"],[292.64,297.85,81,"But it shows that these models are now at a scale that invites the comparison.","但它说明，这些模型如今的规模已经大到让人忍不住去做这种比较。"],[299.1,302.3,82,"Let's make the narrow sense of a language model precise.","我们来精确地定义狭义上的语言模型。"],[302.65,309.08,82,"It's a probabilistic model that assigns a probability to every finite sequence, grammatical or not.","它是一个概率模型，为每一个有限序列赋予概率，无论是否合乎语法。"],[309.43,315.88,82,"Look at the example: the probability of the cat sat on the mat is broken down into a product.","看这个例子：“the cat sat on the mat”的概率被分解成一个乘积。"],[316.23,322.83,82,"P of the, times P of cat given the, times P of sat given the cat, and so on.","P(the) 乘以给定 the 时 cat 的概率，再乘以给定 the cat 时 sat 的概率，依此类推。"],[323.18,327.1,82,"Until finally P of mat, given the cat sat on the.","直到最后，给定 the cat sat on the 时 mat 的概率。"],[327.45,330.31,82,"This is just the chain rule of probability.","这就是概率的链式法则。"],[330.66,337.37,82,"And notice the implicit left-to-right order: each word is predicted from all the words before it.","注意其中隐含的从左到右的顺序：每个词都由它前面的所有词来预测。"],[337.72,341.2,82,"And the punchline: GPT-3 works exactly this way.","而重点是：GPT-3 正是这样工作的。"],[341.55,351.77,82,"The only difference from a textbook n-gram model is how each conditional probability is computed: by a huge neural network with one hundred seventy-five billion parameters.","它和教科书上的 n 元语法模型唯一的区别，在于每个条件概率的计算方式：用一个有 1750 亿参数的巨大神经网络。"],[353.02,357.53,83,"In a broader sense, language model covers three families of architectures.","从广义上讲，语言模型涵盖三类架构。"],[357.88,367.12,83,"Decoder-only models, like the GPT series, generate text left to right, exactly the narrow-sense language model we just saw.","仅解码器模型，比如 GPT 系列，从左到右生成文本，正是我们刚才看到的狭义语言模型。"],[367.47,375.7,83,"Encoder-only models, like BERT, RoBERTa and ELECTRA, read the whole text at once, and are trained differently.","仅编码器模型，比如 BERT、RoBERTa 和 ELECTRA，一次读入整段文本，训练方式也不同。"],[376.05,384.66,83,"Look at the BERT diagram: it masks some words and predicts them using context from both sides, plus a next-sentence prediction task.","看 BERT 的示意图：它遮住一些词，利用两侧的上下文来预测它们，另外还有一个下一句预测任务。"],[385.01,390.3,83,"Encoder-decoder models, like T5 and BART, read an input and generate an output.","编码器-解码器模型，比如 T5 和 BART，读入一个输入，再生成一个输出。"],[390.65,393.84,83,"The T5 diagram shows the text-to-text idea.","T5 的示意图展示了“文本到文本”的思想。"],[394.19,402.15,83,"Translation, grammar judgment, similarity scoring and summarization are all phrased as text in, text out.","翻译、语法判断、相似度打分和摘要，全都表述为输入文本、输出文本。"],[402.5,406.08,83,"The latter two use different pre-training objectives.","后两类使用的是不同的预训练目标。"],[406.43,411.53,83,"Today the decoder-only family dominates, and in a moment we'll see why.","如今仅解码器这一类占据主导，稍后我们就会看到原因。"],[412.78,420.18,84,"You'll hear two terms: PLM, pre-trained language model, and LLM, large language model.","你会听到两个术语：PLM，预训练语言模型；以及 LLM，大语言模型。"],[420.53,424.42,84,"Look at how the slide strikes through pre-trained in LLM.","注意幻灯片上，LLM 里的“pre-trained”被划掉了。"],[424.77,425.67,84,"Why drop it?","为什么去掉它？"],[426.02,435.42,84,"Because for GPT-style models, pre-training and the core training use the same objective, autoregressive next-word prediction.","因为对于 GPT 这类模型，预训练和核心训练使用的是同一个目标：自回归地预测下一个词。"],[435.77,440.07,84,"So pre-trained no longer distinguishes anything. What matters is large.","所以“预训练”已经区分不了什么了。真正重要的是“大”。"],[440.42,446.89,84,"The left chart shows model size on a log scale, from two thousand eighteen to about two thousand twenty-two.","左边的图用对数刻度展示了模型规模，时间从 2018 年到大约 2022 年。"],[447.24,457.37,84,"It goes from ELMo at ninety-four million parameters, through BERT-Large, GPT-2 and T5, to GPT-3 at one hundred seventy-five billion.","从 9400 万参数的 ELMo，经过 BERT-Large、GPT-2 和 T5，到 1750 亿参数的 GPT-3。"],[457.72,461.89,84,"And then Megatron-Turing NLG at five hundred thirty billion.","然后是 5300 亿参数的 Megatron-Turing NLG。"],[462.24,465.5,84,"That's a growth of thousands of times in a few years.","短短几年增长了几千倍。"],[465.85,472.35,84,"The right picture sums up the three ingredients: huge model size, huge data, and huge computing power.","右边的图总结了三大要素：巨大的模型规模、海量的数据和庞大的算力。"],[473.6,478.63,85,"Why did large language models become possible? Because three things are scalable.","大语言模型为什么成为可能？因为有三样东西是可扩展的。"],[478.98,480.87,85,"First, a scalable architecture.","第一，可扩展的架构。"],[481.22,488.13,85,"Transformers parallelize well on GPUs, unlike RNNs, which process words one by one.","Transformer 在 GPU 上能很好地并行，不像 RNN 那样一个词一个词地处理。"],[488.48,490.84,85,"Second, a scalable objective.","第二，可扩展的目标。"],[491.19,499.0,85,"Conditional, autoregressive language modeling turns every position in every text into a training example, with no labels needed.","条件式、自回归的语言建模，把每段文本中的每个位置都变成一个训练样本，完全不需要标注。"],[499.35,500.82,85,"Third, scalable data.","第三，可扩展的数据。"],[501.17,506.16,85,"Plain text is everywhere, while human-labeled data is expensive and scarce.","纯文本随处可见，而人工标注的数据既昂贵又稀缺。"],[506.51,510.99,85,"Projects like MNBVC collect huge Chinese corpora for exactly this reason.","像 MNBVC 这样的项目，正是出于这个原因去收集海量中文语料。"],[511.34,516.02,85,"The chart from the GPT-4 technical report shows why this matters.","GPT-4 技术报告中的这张图说明了这为什么重要。"],[516.37,524.27,85,"The grey dots are smaller training runs; the dashed curve fitted to them predicted GPT-4's final loss, the green dot, before it was trained.","灰点是较小规模的训练；用它们拟合出的虚线，在 GPT-4 训练之前就预测出了它最终的损失，也就是那个绿点。"],[524.62,531.52,85,"When performance follows such a smooth curve with compute, scaling becomes an engineering plan rather than a gamble.","当性能随算力沿着如此平滑的曲线变化时，扩展规模就成了一项工程计划，而不是一场赌博。"],[532.77,535.79,86,"Here's what large means in terms of compute.","这是从算力角度看，“大”意味着什么。"],[536.14,543.26,86,"This chart shows estimated training compute for AI systems over time, in floating-point operations, on a log scale.","这张图展示了 AI 系统训练算力随时间的估计值，单位是浮点运算次数，采用对数刻度。"],[543.61,547.68,86,"Each step up the y-axis is ten thousand times more compute.","纵轴每上升一格，算力就多一万倍。"],[548.03,553.36,86,"Start at the bottom left in the nineteen fifties, with Theseus and ADALINE.","从左下角的二十世纪五十年代开始，有 Theseus 和 ADALINE。"],[553.71,561.9,86,"Then the Neocognitron in nineteen eighty, NetTalk, and the neural probabilistic language model around two thousand.","然后是 1980 年的 Neocognitron、NetTalk，以及 2000 年前后的神经概率语言模型。"],[562.25,572.05,86,"Now look at the top right: BERT-Large, GPT-2, GPT-3, LaMDA, and PaLM at five hundred forty billion parameters.","再看右上角：BERT-Large、GPT-2、GPT-3、LaMDA，还有 5400 亿参数的 PaLM。"],[572.4,576.42,86,"They reach around ten to the twenty-four FLOPs, a yotta FLOP.","它们达到了大约十的二十四次方次浮点运算，也就是一个 yotta FLOP。"],[576.77,580.0,86,"Notice the slope gets much steeper in the last decade.","注意，最近十年曲线的斜率陡峭了许多。"],[580.35,589.6,86,"Compute for frontier models has been growing far faster than it did before deep learning, and that growth is a big part of the LLM story.","前沿模型的算力增长远远快于深度学习之前，而这种增长是大模型故事的重要组成部分。"],[590.85,596.57,87,"Data is the other axis. This chart compares the number of tokens seen during training.","数据是另一个维度。这张图比较了训练中见过的 token 数量。"],[596.92,602.16,87,"A thirteen-year-old human has heard or read fewer than one hundred million words.","一个十三岁的孩子听过或读过的词不到一亿个。"],[602.51,608.02,87,"BERT in two thousand eighteen saw about three billion tokens. RoBERTa, thirty billion.","2018 年的 BERT 见过大约 30 亿个 token。RoBERTa 是 300 亿。"],[608.37,613.37,87,"GPT-3, around two hundred billion. Chinchilla, one point four trillion.","GPT-3 大约是 2000 亿。Chinchilla 是 1.4 万亿。"],[613.72,620.01,87,"And according to the Qwen3 technical report, Qwen3 was trained on thirty-six trillion tokens.","而根据 Qwen3 技术报告，Qwen3 用 36 万亿个 token 进行了训练。"],[620.36,626.41,87,"Think about that gap: models see hundreds of thousands of times more text than a teenager.","想想这个差距：模型看到的文本是一个青少年的几十万倍。"],[626.76,632.17,87,"Yet children are still far more data-efficient learners. That's a deep open question.","然而孩子们在数据利用效率上仍然高得多。这是一个深刻的开放问题。"],[632.52,639.98,87,"The BabyLM challenge, linked at the bottom, asks exactly that: how well can we do with a child-sized amount of data?","底部链接的 BabyLM 挑战赛问的正是这个：只用孩子那么多的数据，我们能做到多好？"],[641.23,644.96,88,"So, how large is large? The answer keeps changing.","那么，多大才算大？答案一直在变。"],[645.31,647.89,88,"A few years ago we talked about two camps.","几年前，我们谈论的是两大阵营。"],[648.24,654.73,88,"Medium-sized models like BERT, RoBERTa and T5, from a hundred million to a few billion parameters.","中等规模的模型，比如 BERT、RoBERTa 和 T5，参数从一亿到几十亿不等。"],[655.08,658.76,88,"And very large models, with a hundred billion parameters or more.","以及超大模型，参数达到一千亿甚至更多。"],[659.11,663.08,88,"Bigger models need more compute, and are more expensive to run.","更大的模型需要更多算力，运行成本也更高。"],[663.43,673.54,88,"They're also used differently: small models are usually fine-tuned, while large ones can be used zero-shot or few-shot, through prompting and in-context learning.","它们的用法也不同：小模型通常要微调，而大模型可以通过提示和上下文学习，以零样本或少样本的方式使用。"],[673.89,680.56,88,"Some abilities seem to emerge only at scale, and there's a trade-off between model size and how much data you train on.","有些能力似乎只在大规模时才会涌现，而且模型大小和训练数据量之间存在权衡。"],[680.91,688.56,88,"The picture is from a famous Chinese comedy sketch about Starbucks cup sizes, where tall turns out to be the small one.","这张图来自一个关于星巴克杯型的著名中文段子，里面“tall”其实是小杯。"],[688.91,690.24,88,"Large is relative.","“大”是相对的。"],[690.59,695.32,88,"And the question mark on rumors like ten trillion parameters is deliberate.","而像“十万亿参数”这类传闻后面打的问号，是有意为之的。"],[695.67,700.81,88,"Frontier labs rarely disclose model sizes, so treat such numbers as speculation.","前沿实验室很少公开模型规模，所以这类数字只能当作猜测。"],[702.06,706.05,89,"We've followed the path from old NLP to large language models.","我们已经沿着从传统 NLP 到大语言模型的道路走了一遍。"],[706.4,710.0,89,"But the story doesn't stop at a model that writes text.","但故事并没有停在一个会写文字的模型上。"],[710.35,715.02,89,"The next step is agents: LLMs that don't just answer, but act.","下一步是智能体：不只是回答问题、还会采取行动的大模型。"],[715.37,723.37,89,"They use tools, operate apps, play games, control robots, and complete multi-step tasks in an environment.","它们会使用工具、操作应用、玩游戏、控制机器人，并在环境中完成多步骤的任务。"],[723.72,725.91,89,"Let me show you three quick examples.","我给大家看三个简短的例子。"],[727.16,729.32,90,"First, a mobile agent.","第一个，手机智能体。"],[729.67,735.38,90,"This demo shows Mobile-Agent, an open-source project, operating a smartphone by itself.","这个演示展示的是开源项目 Mobile-Agent，它可以自己操作智能手机。"],[735.73,743.22,90,"You give it an instruction in natural language, something like: find a restaurant and send the address to a friend.","你用自然语言给它一条指令，比如：找一家餐厅，把地址发给朋友。"],[743.57,753.31,90,"It looks at screenshots of the phone, decides where to tap and what to type, and moves between apps step by step, just like a person would.","它查看手机截图，决定点哪里、输入什么，并一步步在应用之间切换，就像人一样。"],[753.66,762.86,90,"The key idea is that the LLM becomes the brain, the phone screen becomes its eyes, and taps and typing become its hands.","关键思想是：大模型是大脑，手机屏幕是眼睛，点击和输入就是双手。"],[763.21,769.63,90,"That loop of perceive, decide, act is what makes something an agent.","感知、决策、行动这个循环，正是智能体之所以成为智能体的原因。"],[770.88,773.42,91,"Second, a game agent in Minecraft.","第二个，Minecraft 里的游戏智能体。"],[773.77,778.04,91,"The task here is get the obsidian, which takes many steps.","这里的任务是“获取黑曜石”，需要很多步骤。"],[778.39,785.34,91,"Get a water bucket, approach lava, pour water to create obsidian, switch to a diamond pickaxe, and mine it.","拿到一桶水，靠近岩浆，倒水生成黑曜石，换上钻石镐，然后把它挖下来。"],[785.69,787.31,91,"Follow the path around the figure.","沿着图中的路径看一圈。"],[787.66,796.01,91,"At each stage, a high-level reasoner figures out the next subgoal, and points to the exact object in the current view to interact with.","在每个阶段，高层推理模块确定下一个子目标，并在当前画面中指出要交互的具体物体。"],[796.36,799.99,91,"And a lower-level policy carries out the actions.","然后由底层策略执行具体动作。"],[800.34,803.53,91,"The numbered speech bubbles are the agent's own reasoning.","这些带编号的对话气泡，就是智能体自己的推理过程。"],[803.88,813.2,91,"Open-world games like this are a great testbed for agents, because they need long-horizon planning, perception and precise control, all at once.","像这样的开放世界游戏是智能体的绝佳试验场，因为它同时需要长程规划、感知和精确控制。"],[814.45,818.53,92,"Third, embodied AI: an agent with a physical body.","第三个，具身智能：拥有物理身体的智能体。"],[818.88,826.24,92,"This is Mobile ALOHA from Stanford, a two-armed robot on a mobile base, here cooking shrimp autonomously.","这是斯坦福的 Mobile ALOHA，一个装在移动底座上的双臂机器人，正在自主地做虾。"],[826.59,829.06,92,"Note the clip is sped up six times.","注意这段画面是六倍速播放的。"],[829.41,837.6,92,"Cooking needs perception, fine motor control and sequencing: heat the pan, add oil, place the shrimp, flip it, serve it.","做饭需要感知、精细的运动控制和步骤编排：热锅、倒油、放虾、翻面、装盘。"],[837.95,844.17,92,"When you combine robots like this with language models, you can tell a robot what you want in plain words.","当把这样的机器人和语言模型结合起来，你就能用平常的话告诉机器人你想要什么。"],[844.52,853.39,92,"So the arc of today goes from words, to sentences, to language models, to LLMs, to agents acting in digital and physical worlds.","所以今天的脉络是：从词，到句子，到语言模型，到大模型，再到在数字世界和物理世界中行动的智能体。"],[853.74,856.68,92,"That's also roughly the arc of this whole course.","这大致也是整门课程的脉络。"]]},{"n":8,"title":"Research Showcase: Medical, Multilingual and Math LLMs","blurb":"Examples from our group: HuatuoGPT and Apollo for medicine, AceGPT for Arabic, multimodal models, LLMs for math and optimization, and agents interacting with humans.","file":"lecture01_part8.mp4","poster":"lecture01_part8.jpg","duration":674.6,"first":93,"last":110,"slides":[{"n":93,"title":"Contents","t":0.8},{"n":94,"title":"Example I：HuatuoGPT","t":27.93},{"n":95,"title":"华佗GPT智能导诊和预问诊系统以及龙岗家医应用到深圳市龙岗区11家公立医院和186家社康医院，服务500万人口","t":101.33},{"n":96,"title":"Best medical LLMs in Oct. 2023","t":153.29},{"n":97,"title":"Apollo: the multilingual version of Medical LLMs","t":212.48},{"n":98,"title":"Arabic LLMs AceGPT： value alignment for a new language (Arabic) AceGPT 1.5: vocabulary expansion AceGPT 2: native alignm","t":264.43},{"n":99,"title":"Slide 99","t":320.47},{"n":100,"title":"Example III ：Multi-modal LLMs","t":362.41},{"n":103,"title":"Example IV：LLM for Math and Optimization","t":419.01},{"n":104,"title":"https://paperswithcode.com/sota/arithmetic-reasoning-on-gsm8k","t":474.01},{"n":105,"title":"在2025年第二届人工智能数学奥林匹克竞赛（AIMO2）中荣获金牌 联合杉数科技开发首个数学建模大模型 ORLM，并由该公司进一步升级为 COLORMind 平台投入实际业务应用。ORLM 的研究论文被国际顶级期刊《Operations R","t":526.73},{"n":106,"title":"Example V：Agent and Human-Agent Interactions","t":573.57},{"n":107,"title":"Example V：Agent and Human-Agent Interactions","t":637.11}],"sents":[[0.8,4.8,93,"That wraps up our tour of NLP and large language models.","关于 NLP 和大语言模型的介绍就到这里。"],[5.15,11.86,93,"We went from what NLP is, through its history, to language modeling, LLMs and agents.","我们从 NLP 是什么讲起，经过它的历史，一直讲到语言建模、大模型和智能体。"],[12.21,16.07,93,"In the last part, I'd like to show you some research from our own group.","在最后一部分，我想给大家展示一些我们自己课题组的研究。"],[16.42,22.74,93,"The question here is: what can a university research team actually build with these ideas?","这里的问题是：一个大学研究团队，用这些思想到底能做出什么？"],[23.09,26.53,93,"I hope it gives you some inspiration for your own projects.","希望它能为你们自己的项目带来一些启发。"],[27.78,37.17,94,"Our first example is HuatuoGPT, our line of medical language models, named after Hua Tuo, the famous ancient Chinese physician.","第一个例子是华佗GPT，也就是我们的医疗语言模型系列，以中国古代名医华佗命名。"],[37.52,42.12,94,"Read the timeline as a story of one research direction growing step by step.","请把这条时间线看作一个研究方向一步步成长的故事。"],[42.47,48.48,94,"We started in two thousand twenty-three with HuatuoGPT, a model taught to behave like a doctor.","我们在 2023 年从 HuatuoGPT 开始，这是一个被教会像医生一样行事的模型。"],[48.83,54.22,94,"Along with it came Huatuo-26M, a very large medical QA dataset.","与之一起推出的还有 Huatuo-26M，一个非常大的医疗问答数据集。"],[54.57,61.01,94,"Then HuatuoGPT-II simplified medical adaptation into a one-stage training process.","随后，HuatuoGPT-II 把医疗领域适配简化为一个单阶段的训练过程。"],[61.36,67.41,94,"Apollo extended medical LLMs to multiple languages, first six, and later fifty.","Apollo 把医疗大模型扩展到多种语言，先是六种，后来是五十种。"],[67.76,71.24,94,"HuatuoGPT-Vision added medical images.","HuatuoGPT-Vision 加入了医学影像。"],[71.59,75.47,94,"HuatuoGPT-o1 tackled complex medical reasoning.","HuatuoGPT-o1 攻克了复杂的医学推理。"],[75.82,83.4,94,"And TCM-omni brings multimodal models, with audio, vision and EEG, to traditional Chinese medicine.","TCM-omni 则把融合音频、视觉和脑电的多模态模型带进了中医领域。"],[83.75,88.83,94,"And we went beyond papers: the system was deployed in twelve local hospitals.","而且我们不止于论文：这个系统已经部署到了 12 家本地医院。"],[89.18,99.93,94,"The lesson for your projects: pick a domain you care about, and keep pushing it along new axes: data, languages, modalities, reasoning, deployment.","对你们项目的启示是：选一个你关心的领域，然后沿着新的维度不断推进：数据、语言、模态、推理、部署。"],[101.18,103.94,95,"This is where research meets the real world.","这就是研究与真实世界相遇的地方。"],[104.29,111.19,95,"On the left is the launch ceremony of the HuatuoGPT-based intelligent triage and pre-consultation system.","左边是基于华佗GPT的智能导诊和预问诊系统的上线仪式。"],[111.54,118.56,95,"According to the slide, together with a family-doctor application, it's used across Longgang District in Shenzhen.","根据幻灯片，它和一个家庭医生应用一起，在深圳市龙岗区投入使用。"],[118.91,126.05,95,"That's eleven public hospitals and one hundred eighty-six community health centers, serving a population of about five million.","覆盖 11 家公立医院和 186 家社区健康服务中心，服务大约 500 万人口。"],[126.4,129.99,95,"On the right is a world map showing the languages Apollo covers.","右边是一张世界地图，展示了 Apollo 覆盖的语言。"],[130.34,137.8,95,"Extended to fifty languages, it aims to bring medical AI to people who speak languages that big companies often ignore.","扩展到五十种语言后，它希望把医疗 AI 带给那些说着常被大公司忽视的语言的人们。"],[138.15,144.37,95,"According to the slide, that reaches a combined population of nearly eight billion people worldwide.","根据幻灯片，这覆盖了全球近 80 亿人口。"],[144.72,151.89,95,"For me, this is what makes NLP exciting: a model trained in a university lab can end up helping patients.","对我来说，这正是 NLP 激动人心的地方：一个在大学实验室里训练出的模型，最终能帮助到病人。"],[153.14,154.97,96,"Here's how well it performed.","来看看它的表现有多好。"],[155.32,165.57,96,"This table compares models on China's two thousand twenty-three Pharmacist Licensure Examination, in both the Western pharmacy track and the traditional Chinese medicine track.","这张表比较了各模型在 2023 年中国执业药师资格考试上的成绩，包括西药和中药两个方向。"],[165.92,172.97,96,"The bottom rows are our HuatuoGPT-II models, at seven, thirteen and thirty-four billion parameters.","最下面几行是我们的 HuatuoGPT-II 模型，参数分别为 70 亿、130 亿和 340 亿。"],[173.32,176.08,96,"Compare the average column on the far right.","对比一下最右边的平均分一栏。"],[176.43,186.65,96,"The thirty-four billion model scored sixty-four point zero, higher than GPT-4 at forty-eight point one, and the other general models of that time.","340 亿参数的模型得了 64.0 分，高于 GPT-4 的 48.1 分，也高于当时其他通用模型。"],[187.0,194.63,96,"The note under the table says, roughly, that a November model was tested on an October exam.","表格下方的说明大意是：用十一月的模型去考十月的考试。"],[194.98,200.67,96,"The exam had just happened, so its questions couldn't have leaked into the training data.","考试刚刚结束，所以题目不可能泄漏到训练数据里。"],[201.02,211.08,96,"That's a clean test, and an important habit in evaluation: always worry about whether your test set was seen during training.","这是一次干净的测试，也是评测中的一个重要习惯：永远要警惕测试集是否在训练中被见过。"],[212.33,214.7,97,"Apollo is the multilingual version.","Apollo 是多语言版本。"],[215.05,224.96,97,"The idea is to democratize medical AI: most medical models work well in English and maybe Chinese, but billions of people speak other languages.","它的理念是让医疗 AI 普惠大众：多数医疗模型只在英语、也许还有中文上表现好，但有数十亿人说的是其他语言。"],[225.31,233.18,97,"This table compares models on medical question answering across English, Chinese, French, Spanish, Arabic and Hindi.","这张表比较了各模型在英语、中文、法语、西班牙语、阿拉伯语和印地语上的医疗问答表现。"],[233.53,240.9,97,"Look at the bottom block, our Apollo models, from zero point five billion up to seventy-two billion parameters.","看最下面这一块，是我们的 Apollo 模型，参数从 5 亿到 720 亿。"],[241.25,247.12,97,"Apollo-72B has the highest average in this table, slightly above GPT-4.","Apollo-72B 的平均分是这张表中最高的，略高于 GPT-4。"],[247.47,252.74,97,"And even the small models are competitive with much larger open models.","即使是小模型，也能和大得多的开源模型一较高下。"],[253.09,263.03,97,"Small, multilingual and lightweight matters a lot in medicine, because hospitals often need to run models locally, for privacy and cost reasons.","小巧、多语言、轻量化在医疗领域非常重要，因为出于隐私和成本考虑，医院常常需要在本地运行模型。"],[264.28,270.34,98,"Our second example is about language rather than domain: building LLMs for Arabic.","第二个例子关乎语言而不是领域：为阿拉伯语构建大模型。"],[270.69,276.61,98,"Arabic is spoken by hundreds of millions of people, but was underserved by early LLMs.","阿拉伯语有数亿使用者，但早期的大模型对它的支持很不够。"],[276.96,279.39,98,"So we built the AceGPT series.","于是我们构建了 AceGPT 系列。"],[279.74,290.04,98,"The first version focused on value alignment: making the model fit the culture and values of Arabic-speaking users, not just translating English values.","第一版专注于价值对齐：让模型契合阿拉伯语用户的文化和价值观，而不只是翻译英语世界的价值观。"],[290.39,297.74,98,"AceGPT one point five expanded the vocabulary, so the model represents Arabic text more efficiently.","AceGPT 1.5 扩充了词表，让模型能更高效地表示阿拉伯语文本。"],[298.09,306.22,98,"AceGPT two explored native alignment, building alignment in during pre-training rather than only afterward.","AceGPT 2 探索了原生对齐，在预训练阶段就融入对齐，而不只是事后再做。"],[306.57,312.16,98,"According to the slide, at release AceGPT was the best Arabic LLM.","根据幻灯片，AceGPT 发布时是最好的阿拉伯语大模型。"],[312.51,319.07,98,"The general lesson: a language isn't just a different set of tokens; it comes with its own culture.","普遍的启示是：一种语言不只是一套不同的 token，它还承载着自己的文化。"],[320.32,325.06,99,"This project drew international attention, and not all of it was technical.","这个项目引起了国际关注，而且并不全是技术层面的。"],[325.41,336.14,99,"On the left is a Financial Times article about the collaboration between King Abdullah University of Science and Technology in Saudi Arabia and CUHK-Shenzhen on AceGPT.","左边是《金融时报》的一篇文章，讲的是沙特阿卜杜拉国王科技大学与港中大（深圳）在 AceGPT 上的合作。"],[336.49,339.73,99,"It raised concerns about access to AI chips.","文章对 AI 芯片的获取提出了担忧。"],[340.08,344.11,99,"On the right is a Chinese news report responding to that coverage.","右边是一篇回应该报道的中文新闻。"],[344.46,348.84,99,"I'm showing this to remind you that AI research doesn't happen in a vacuum.","我展示这个是想提醒大家：AI 研究不是在真空中进行的。"],[349.19,356.05,99,"Large models depend on chips, data and international collaboration, and that makes them part of geopolitics.","大模型依赖芯片、数据和国际合作，这使它们成为地缘政治的一部分。"],[356.4,361.01,99,"As NLP researchers, you'll increasingly need to be aware of that context.","作为 NLP 研究者，你们会越来越需要了解这样的背景。"],[362.26,371.23,100,"Our third example is multimodal LLMs: models that handle images, video, motion and speech, not just text.","第三个例子是多模态大模型：不只处理文本，还能处理图像、视频、动作和语音的模型。"],[371.58,373.1,100,"A quick tour of the list.","我们快速过一下这份清单。"],[373.45,378.75,100,"ALLaVA, a high-quality image-text dataset and a lite vision-language model.","ALLaVA，一个高质量的图文数据集，以及一个轻量的视觉语言模型。"],[379.1,385.51,100,"A benchmark for long-context multimodal models, accepted at COLM two thousand twenty-four.","一个面向长上下文多模态模型的评测基准，被 COLM 2024 接收。"],[385.86,394.04,100,"MotionLLM, for understanding human motion, and MLLM-Bench, for evaluating multimodal models.","MotionLLM，用于理解人体动作；MLLM-Bench，用于评测多模态模型。"],[394.39,397.25,100,"Feedback learning for multimodal models.","多模态大模型的反馈学习。"],[397.6,403.33,100,"Soundwave for speech understanding, and Echo-X, an end-to-end speech model.","用于语音理解的 Soundwave，以及端到端语音大模型 Echo-X。"],[403.68,407.5,100,"And Janus, image generation based on language models.","还有 Janus，基于语言模型的图像生成。"],[407.85,412.66,100,"The common thread: language serves as the hub that connects all these modalities.","它们的共同主线是：语言作为枢纽，把所有这些模态连接起来。"],[413.01,417.61,100,"We'll go into this properly in the multimodal lecture later in the semester.","我们会在本学期后面的多模态专题课上详细讲。"],[418.86,423.46,103,"Our fourth example is LLMs for math and optimization.","第四个例子是用于数学和优化的大模型。"],[423.81,424.98,103,"A few highlights.","挑几个亮点。"],[425.33,432.15,103,"MathScale, at ICML two thousand twenty-four, scaled up instruction-tuning data for mathematical reasoning.","MathScale 发表于 ICML 2024，它扩大了面向数学推理的指令微调数据规模。"],[432.5,443.35,103,"ORLM trains LLMs to do optimization modeling, turning a business problem described in words into a mathematical model that a solver can handle.","ORLM 训练大模型做优化建模，把用文字描述的业务问题转化成求解器能处理的数学模型。"],[443.7,449.3,103,"And it was published in Operations Research, a top journal in that field.","它发表在该领域的顶级期刊《Operations Research》上。"],[449.65,452.3,103,"Mamo is a benchmark for mathematical modeling.","Mamo 是一个数学建模的评测基准。"],[452.65,457.61,103,"OVM uses outcome-supervised value models to guide step-by-step math reasoning.","OVM 用结果监督的价值模型来引导逐步的数学推理。"],[457.96,463.23,103,"And there's work on synthetic data, and on teaching models through Socratic questioning.","还有关于合成数据，以及通过苏格拉底式提问来教模型的工作。"],[463.58,468.03,103,"Math is a great testbed, because answers can be checked exactly.","数学是很好的试验场，因为答案可以被精确验证。"],[468.38,472.61,103,"That makes it the ideal playground for reasoning research.","这使它成为推理研究的理想舞台。"],[473.86,475.72,104,"Here's one concrete result.","来看一个具体的结果。"],[476.07,485.24,104,"This is a GSM8K leaderboard snapshot; GSM8K is a widely used benchmark of grade-school math word problems.","这是 GSM8K 排行榜的截图；GSM8K 是一个广泛使用的小学数学应用题基准。"],[485.59,488.99,104,"The top rows are mostly GPT-4 variants.","排在最前面的大多是 GPT-4 的各种变体。"],[489.34,497.87,104,"But look at the rows boxed in red: seven-billion-parameter Mistral models fine-tuned with our methods, including OVM.","但看红框标出的几行：用我们的方法，包括 OVM，微调过的 70 亿参数 Mistral 模型。"],[498.22,503.85,104,"They score around ninety-five to ninety-six percent, in the same range as GPT-4 setups.","它们的得分在 95% 到 96% 左右，和 GPT-4 的各种配置处于同一水平。"],[504.2,508.54,104,"And they're even ahead of some well-known commercial models further down.","甚至还领先于下面一些知名的商业模型。"],[508.89,519.35,104,"The message: with the right training data and the right verification method, a small open model can compete with a giant one on a specific task.","要传达的是：有了合适的训练数据和验证方法，一个小的开源模型可以在特定任务上与巨型模型一较高下。"],[519.7,525.33,104,"That's very relevant to your final projects, since you won't have GPT-4-scale compute.","这对你们的期末项目非常有参考价值，因为你们不会有 GPT-4 级别的算力。"],[526.58,528.85,105,"Two more achievements on the math side.","数学方面还有两项成果。"],[529.2,539.8,105,"First, according to the slide, a team won a gold medal at the second AI Mathematical Olympiad Progress Prize, AIMO2, in two thousand twenty-five.","第一，根据幻灯片，一支团队在 2025 年第二届人工智能数学奥林匹克竞赛 AIMO2 中获得金牌。"],[540.15,547.08,105,"That competition asks AI systems to solve olympiad-level problems under strict compute limits.","这项比赛要求 AI 系统在严格的算力限制下解决奥赛级别的题目。"],[547.43,554.79,105,"Second, ORLM was developed together with the company Cardinal Operations, known in Chinese as Shanshu Technology.","第二，ORLM 是与杉数科技公司联合开发的。"],[555.14,559.86,105,"It was the first large model for mathematical modeling in optimization.","它是首个面向优化领域数学建模的大模型。"],[560.21,568.28,105,"The company upgraded it into a platform called COLORMind for real business use, and the paper was published in Operations Research.","该公司把它升级为 COLORMind 平台，投入实际业务应用，相关论文也发表在《Operations Research》上。"],[568.63,572.17,105,"It shows a full path from paper to product.","这展示了一条从论文到产品的完整路径。"],[573.42,579.4,106,"Our fifth example is agents and human-agent interaction, starting with TwinMarket.","第五个例子是智能体以及人与智能体的交互，先从 TwinMarket 说起。"],[579.75,586.54,106,"TwinMarket simulates a financial market with many LLM-powered agents, each acting like an individual investor.","TwinMarket 用许多由大模型驱动的智能体来模拟金融市场，每个智能体都像一个个体投资者。"],[586.89,590.82,106,"Follow the figure: each agent has a user profile and beliefs.","看这张图：每个智能体都有用户画像和信念。"],[591.17,598.06,106,"It gathers world knowledge from news, stock data and returns, then forms desires and intentions.","它从新闻、股票数据和收益中获取世界知识，然后形成欲望和意图。"],[598.41,604.65,106,"Then it acts, by trading, and by posting, liking or reposting on a social network.","然后它采取行动：进行交易，并在社交网络上发帖、点赞或转发。"],[605.0,612.25,106,"Those social interactions spread opinions and even rumors, which feed back into beliefs and the market.","这些社交互动传播着观点甚至谣言，又反过来影响信念和市场。"],[612.6,617.74,106,"The exciting part is that, with many such agents, you can study emergent social phenomena.","令人兴奋的是，有了大量这样的智能体，你就能研究涌现出来的社会现象。"],[618.09,625.07,106,"For example, how rumors trigger bubbles or crashes, which are hard to study with real people.","比如谣言如何引发泡沫或崩盘，而这些用真人是很难研究的。"],[625.42,635.71,106,"This work won the best paper award at the ICLR two thousand twenty-five Financial AI workshop, and appeared at NeurIPS two thousand twenty-five.","这项工作获得了 ICLR 2025 金融 AI 研讨会的最佳论文奖，并发表在 NeurIPS 2025 上。"],[636.96,640.36,107,"Here's a more playful example of human-agent interaction.","这是一个更有趣的人与智能体交互的例子。"],[640.71,644.51,107,"This is our campus, CUHK-Shenzhen, rebuilt in Minecraft.","这是在 Minecraft 里重建的我们的校园，港中大（深圳）。"],[644.86,647.07,107,"On the left you can see the buildings.","左边可以看到校园的建筑。"],[647.42,655.15,107,"On the right, as you walk around, you meet an AI-driven character of Professor Luo Zhiquan, one of our university leaders.","右边，当你四处走动时，会遇到一个由 AI 驱动的罗智泉教授的角色，他是我们学校的领导之一。"],[655.5,659.7,107,"He welcomes you to campus, and you can chat with him or ask for clues.","他欢迎你来到校园，你可以和他聊天，或者向他寻求线索。"],[660.05,662.71,107,"It's fun, but there's a serious idea underneath.","这很好玩，但背后有一个严肃的想法。"],[663.06,672.71,107,"Game worlds populated by LLM-powered characters are great environments for studying how people and agents interact, and for building educational experiences.","由大模型驱动的角色组成的游戏世界，是研究人与智能体如何交互、以及打造教育体验的绝佳环境。"]]},{"n":9,"title":"Recursive Self-Improvement, Oversight and Your Views","blurb":"Where the group's research is heading: recursive self-improvement in heterogeneous real-world environments, the challenge of scalable oversight, and class surveys on AI, jobs and law.","file":"lecture01_part9.mp4","poster":"lecture01_part9.jpg","duration":505.4,"first":111,"last":122,"slides":[{"n":111,"title":"Our research","t":0.8},{"n":113,"title":"Recursive Self-improvement (RSI)","t":47.16},{"n":114,"title":"Challenge： Scalable oversight！","t":97.28},{"n":115,"title":"Applications (heterogeneous environments )","t":144.8},{"n":116,"title":"Surveys","t":241.76},{"n":117,"title":"Survey 1：Jobs in the future","t":260.1},{"n":118,"title":"Survey 2：Intelligence Law","t":300.57},{"n":119,"title":"Survey 3: AI replaced Humans?","t":341.43},{"n":120,"title":"Survey 4: AI replaced Humans?","t":377.09},{"n":121,"title":"Thanks Join us as a RA if interested","t":413.29},{"n":122,"title":"Survey","t":479.65}],"sents":[[0.8,3.44,111,"So where is our research heading next?","那么，我们的研究接下来往哪里走？"],[3.79,10.5,111,"If I had to summarize it in one line: recursive self-improvement in heterogeneous real-world environments.","如果要用一句话概括：在异构的真实世界环境中实现递归自我改进。"],[10.85,21.0,111,"Recursive self-improvement, or RSI, means an AI system that helps produce better versions of itself, through better data, better training, better tools.","递归自我改进，简称 RSI，指的是 AI 系统通过更好的数据、更好的训练、更好的工具，帮助产生更好版本的自己。"],[21.35,27.85,111,"Heterogeneous real-world environments means we want this to happen not just in clean benchmarks like math.","异构的真实世界环境，是指我们希望这不只发生在像数学这样干净的基准上。"],[28.2,34.38,111,"We want it in messy settings too, like hospitals, financial markets and the physical world.","也要发生在复杂混乱的场景中，比如医院、金融市场和物理世界。"],[34.73,42.69,111,"Remember the former TA I mentioned at the beginning, who wants to start a company on RSI? This is the direction he's excited about too.","还记得我在开头提到的那位想做 RSI 创业的前助教吗？这也是他为之兴奋的方向。"],[43.04,45.76,111,"Let me unpack it in a couple of slides.","我用几页幻灯片来展开讲讲。"],[47.01,49.99,113,"Here's the picture behind recursive self-improvement.","这是递归自我改进背后的图景。"],[50.34,55.56,113,"Imagine we've built a super AI, stronger than all humans combined at some set of tasks.","想象我们已经造出了一个超级 AI，在某些任务上比全人类加起来还强。"],[55.91,61.47,113,"The natural next question, for it or for us, is: how can I make it even stronger?","接下来自然要问的问题，无论是它问还是我们问，都是：怎样让它变得更强？"],[61.82,70.55,113,"If the AI itself becomes the best engineer for improving AI, then each generation helps build the next, and progress could compound.","如果 AI 本身成了改进 AI 的最佳工程师，那么每一代都会帮助构建下一代，进步就可能不断叠加。"],[70.9,77.27,113,"That loop is what people mean by RSI, and it's one of the paths people discuss toward superintelligence.","这个循环就是人们所说的 RSI，也是人们讨论的通向超级智能的路径之一。"],[77.62,80.95,113,"Whether and how fast this happens is debated.","这是否会发生、会多快发生，仍有争论。"],[81.3,90.66,113,"But even partial versions, like models generating their own training data or verifying each other's work, are already standard practice.","但即使是部分形式，比如模型生成自己的训练数据，或者相互验证彼此的结果，都已经是标准做法了。"],[91.01,95.88,113,"You'll see examples when we talk about LLM training and reinforcement learning.","等我们讲到大模型训练和强化学习时，你们会看到例子。"],[97.13,101.42,114,"And here's the biggest challenge that RSI raises: scalable oversight.","而 RSI 带来的最大挑战是：可扩展监督。"],[101.77,106.83,114,"Look at the left side. In traditional oversight, humans supervise the AI.","看左边。在传统的监督方式中，由人类来监督 AI。"],[107.18,115.3,114,"But as the AI's capability grows, the grey bars, human supervisory capacity stays flat, the red dashed line.","但随着 AI 能力增长，也就是灰色柱子，人类的监督能力却保持不变，也就是红色虚线。"],[115.65,122.67,114,"Human time and attention are limited, we can't keep up, and oversight becomes the ceiling of the whole system.","人类的时间和注意力有限，跟不上模型的增长，监督就成了整个系统的天花板。"],[123.02,125.89,114,"The right side shows the goal: oversight that scales.","右边展示的是目标：可以扩展的监督。"],[126.24,135.43,114,"AI helps generate feedback, evaluate and monitor, so our ability to supervise grows together with model capability, the green bars.","AI 协助生成反馈、进行评估和监控，让我们的监督能力随模型能力一起增长，也就是绿色柱子。"],[135.78,143.4,114,"How to do this reliably is one of the most important open problems in AI, both for safety and for continued progress.","如何可靠地做到这一点，是 AI 领域最重要的开放问题之一，无论对安全还是对持续进步都是如此。"],[144.65,149.94,115,"So what can recursive self-improvement look like in practice? There are several forms.","那么，递归自我改进在实践中是什么样子？它有几种形式。"],[150.29,158.44,115,"The simplest is self-improvement: a model at step t gathers experience and data, and that produces a better model at step t plus one.","最简单的是自我改进：第 t 步的模型积累经验和数据，由此产生第 t 加 1 步更好的模型。"],[158.79,167.77,115,"Then there is mutual improvement between two models, such as a solver and a verifier, or a generator and a solver, each making the other better.","然后是两个模型之间的相互改进，比如求解器和验证器，或者生成器和求解器，彼此促进。"],[168.12,176.65,115,"In co-evolution, the model improves together with its harness, its environment, a world model, or the humans it works with.","在协同进化中，模型与它的运行框架、环境、世界模型，或与之合作的人类一同改进。"],[177.0,184.53,115,"Population evolution keeps many models, mutates and searches, and selects the best to form a stronger population.","种群进化则维护许多模型，通过变异和搜索，再选出最好的，形成更强的种群。"],[184.88,192.14,115,"And at the system level, the model builds better tools, compilers, data and environments, which then produce a better model.","而在系统层面，模型构建出更好的工具、编译器、数据和环境，进而产生更好的模型。"],[192.49,201.38,115,"That last form is the most truly recursive, because the AI is improving the very machinery that produces the next generation of AI.","最后这种形式最具递归意味，因为 AI 改进的正是产生下一代 AI 的那台“机器”。"],[201.73,211.07,115,"So I define RSI broadly: an intelligent system improves not only its own policy, but also the mechanisms that produce its future improvements.","所以我对 RSI 的定义更宽泛：智能系统不仅改进自身的策略，还改进产生其未来改进的机制。"],[211.42,215.91,115,"And we want to do this in heterogeneous environments, listed here.","而我们希望在这里列出的这些异构环境中实现它。"],[216.26,221.55,115,"In healthcare: an agentic hospital, medical world models, and virtual cells.","在医疗领域：智能体医院、医学世界模型和虚拟细胞。"],[221.9,227.5,115,"In AI for AI: kernel optimization and automatic architecture design.","在用 AI 改进 AI 方面：算子内核优化和自动架构设计。"],[227.85,233.53,115,"In finance and law: quantitative finance and corporate finance.","在金融和法律应用方面：量化金融和公司金融。"],[233.88,240.36,115,"And world models, both interactive and three-D, plus games and embodied AI.","还有世界模型，包括交互式和三维的世界模型，以及游戏和具身智能。"],[241.61,242.8,116,"We're near the end.","我们快要结束了。"],[243.15,247.35,116,"Before we finish, I'd like you to think through a few quick survey questions.","结束之前，我想请大家思考几个简短的调查问题。"],[247.7,249.34,116,"There are no right answers here.","这些问题没有标准答案。"],[249.69,258.7,116,"I'm curious about your intuitions about AI and the future of work, and I'll ask similar questions later in the course to see whether your views change.","我很好奇大家对 AI 和未来工作的直觉判断，课程后面我还会问类似的问题，看看大家的看法是否改变。"],[259.95,265.1,117,"First survey: which of these jobs are least likely to be replaced by AI?","第一个调查：下面哪些职业最不容易被 AI 取代？"],[265.45,273.01,117,"Doctors, mathematicians, farmers, software engineers, AI engineers, blue-collar workers, white-collar workers.","医生、数学家、农民、软件工程师、AI 工程师、蓝领工人、白领工人。"],[273.36,275.62,117,"Pick one or two, and think about why.","选一两个，想想为什么。"],[275.97,285.63,117,"Is it because the job needs physical skill? Human trust and responsibility? Creativity? Or because AI is still weak at that kind of reasoning?","是因为这份工作需要身体技能？需要人的信任和责任？需要创造力？还是因为 AI 在那类推理上仍然薄弱？"],[285.98,293.74,117,"Interestingly, a few years ago most people said creative and intellectual jobs were safest, and manual jobs most at risk.","有意思的是，几年前大多数人认为创意型和脑力型工作最安全，体力劳动最危险。"],[294.09,299.17,117,"LLMs have made many people rethink that ordering. What do you think?","大模型让很多人重新思考这个排序。你怎么看？"],[300.42,304.76,118,"Second survey, about what I'd call an intelligence law.","第二个调查，关于我称之为“智能定律”的问题。"],[305.11,312.3,118,"Today, how much work can AI complete at a decent quality level, measured by how long it would take the best humans to do it?","目前，AI 能以像样的质量完成多少工作？用最优秀的人类完成它所需的时间来衡量。"],[312.65,319.76,118,"Less than a minute, one minute to an hour, one to ten hours, ten to a hundred hours, or more than a hundred hours?","少于一分钟、一分钟到一小时、一到十小时、十到一百小时，还是超过一百小时？"],[320.11,329.75,118,"Measuring AI by the length of tasks it can complete is a nice way to track progress, because it's intuitive and comparable over time.","用 AI 能完成的任务时长来衡量它，是追踪进展的好方法，因为它直观，并且可以跨时间比较。"],[330.1,335.47,118,"There have been attempts to measure this kind of task horizon, and it seems to be growing quickly.","已经有人尝试衡量这种“任务时长”，而它似乎正在快速增长。"],[335.82,340.03,118,"Make your guess. We'll revisit this question when we discuss agents.","猜一猜吧。等我们讲智能体时会再回到这个问题。"],[341.28,347.28,119,"Third survey: by two thousand thirty, how much of human work do you think AI will replace?","第三个调查：到 2030 年，你认为 AI 会取代多少人类工作？"],[347.63,355.58,119,"Less than twenty percent, twenty to fifty, fifty to eighty, eighty to ninety-five, more than ninety-five, or all of it?","少于 20%、20% 到 50%、50% 到 80%、80% 到 95%、超过 95%，还是全部？"],[355.93,358.69,119,"Before you answer, think about what replace means.","回答之前，先想想“取代”是什么意思。"],[359.04,364.24,119,"Replacing whole jobs is different from automating many tasks within a job.","取代整份工作，和把一份工作中的许多任务自动化，是不一样的。"],[364.59,368.95,119,"A doctor's job may change a lot, even if doctors still exist.","即使医生这个职业仍然存在，医生的工作内容也可能发生巨大变化。"],[369.3,375.69,119,"There's no consensus among experts here, so your guess is as good as anyone's. Just commit to an answer.","专家们对此没有共识，所以你的猜测和任何人的一样有分量。大胆给出你的答案吧。"],[376.94,383.73,120,"And the same question, but for two thousand fifty. How much of human work will AI replace by then?","同样的问题，但换成 2050 年。到那时 AI 会取代多少人类工作？"],[384.08,388.56,120,"Compare your two answers. Did you choose a much bigger number for two thousand fifty?","比较一下你的两个答案。你给 2050 年选的数字是不是大得多？"],[388.91,393.35,120,"How big is the jump you expect between two thousand thirty and two thousand fifty?","你预期从 2030 年到 2050 年会有多大的跃升？"],[393.7,400.34,120,"And what drives it in your mind: better models, robots, cheaper compute, or social change?","在你看来，推动它的是什么：更好的模型、机器人、更便宜的算力，还是社会变革？"],[400.69,409.42,120,"Whatever you answered, one thing is clear: the people who understand how these systems work will help shape that future, rather than just react to it.","无论你怎么回答，有一点是明确的：懂得这些系统如何运作的人，将参与塑造那个未来，而不只是被动应对。"],[409.77,411.89,120,"That's a big reason this course exists.","这正是开设这门课的一个重要原因。"],[413.14,415.3,121,"Thank you all. Let me wrap up today.","谢谢大家。我来总结一下今天的内容。"],[415.65,417.22,121,"We covered three things.","我们讲了三件事。"],[417.57,426.61,121,"First, how this course works: assignments, and above all the final project, which is worth more than half your grade, so start thinking about it now.","第一，这门课怎么上：作业，尤其是期末项目，它占总成绩的一半以上，所以现在就开始考虑吧。"],[426.96,436.32,121,"Second, what NLP is, and how the field moved from rules and pipelines, to statistical and neural models, to Transformers.","第二，NLP 是什么，以及这个领域如何从规则和流水线，走到统计模型和神经网络模型，再到 Transformer。"],[436.67,444.82,121,"Third, the key idea behind modern LLMs: a language model predicts the next word given the previous words.","第三，现代大模型背后的核心思想：语言模型根据前面的词预测下一个词。"],[445.17,454.78,121,"When you scale that simple objective up with Transformers, huge data and huge compute, you get today's LLMs, and, built on them, agents.","当你用 Transformer、海量数据和庞大算力把这个简单目标扩展开来，就得到了今天的大模型，以及构建在它们之上的智能体。"],[455.13,462.75,121,"Next week, in Lecture two, we go back to the foundations: basics of linguistics and word representation.","下周的第二讲，我们回到基础：语言学基础与词表示。"],[463.1,469.2,121,"How is language structured, and how do we turn words into vectors a machine can compute with?","语言是如何构成的？我们又如何把词变成机器可以计算的向量？"],[469.55,472.07,121,"That's also the theory behind Assignment one.","这也是作业一背后的理论。"],[472.42,478.25,121,"And if you're interested in research, join us as an RA. My email is on the slide.","如果你对研究感兴趣，欢迎加入我们做研究助理。我的邮箱就在幻灯片上。"],[479.5,484.22,122,"Before you go, please scan this QR code and fill in the short survey.","离开之前，请扫描这个二维码，填写一份简短的问卷。"],[484.57,493.55,122,"It helps us understand your background and what you hope to get from the course, so we can adjust the pace and the examples.","它能帮助我们了解你的背景，以及你希望从这门课中收获什么，这样我们就能调整节奏和例子。"],[493.9,499.56,122,"Also, if you haven't joined the WeChat group or bookmarked the course website yet, please do it today.","另外，如果你还没有加入微信群，或者还没收藏课程网站，请今天就完成。"],[499.91,503.59,122,"Thank you, and see you next week for Lecture two. Goodbye!","谢谢大家，下周第二讲再见。再见！"]]}]};
